(* Beginning of Notebook Content *)
Notebook[{
Cell["Boson Sampling Explained", "Title",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
Hong-Ou-Mandel Interference, Multiport Interferometers, Permanents, and the \
Classical Cost of Simulating Identical Photons: A Guided, Computation-First \
Narrative with the Wolfram Language and QuantumFramework\
\>", "Subtitle",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["Mads Bahrami (last updated: Sep 27, 2026)", "Author",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell["Wolfram Research Inc, USA", "Affiliation",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],

Cell["Setting the Stage: How This Notebook Flows", "Subsection",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This notebook is a computation-first tour of boson sampling: how two \
identical photons meeting at a beam splitter leave together (the \
Hong-Ou-Mandel effect), how the photons' distinguishability switches that \
effect off, how any passive optical network is assembled from beam splitters \
and phase shifters, how the amplitude for a pattern of photon detections \
becomes the permanent of a matrix, why some patterns are exactly forbidden, \
and why the cost of simulating identical photons on a classical computer \
grows so quickly. Along the way we simulate the photons directly in their \
Fock space with the second-quantization tools of ",
 ButtonBox["QuantumFramework",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://resources.wolframcloud.com/PacletRepository/resources/\
Wolfram/QuantumFramework/"], None}],
 " (Fock states, beam splitters, phase shifters, quantum circuits, and a \
symbolic algebra of creation and annihilation operators), and we cross-check \
every result against the permanent formula and against two computations \
written in plain Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],

Cell["\<\
In other words, I've tried to build a catalogue of computational experiments \
on identical photons, tools and examples that let you run the experiments \
yourself and learn directly from what you observe. I strongly believe in a \
computation-first narrative for learning: in a sense, if I cannot compute it, \
I cannot claim to understand it.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before we start, pay attention to a few things. The environment you see is \
a ",
 ButtonBox["Wolfram (Mathematica) notebook",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://www.wolfram.com/notebooks/"], None}],
 ". You should evaluate the cells from top to bottom. Although I did my best \
to make the input cells independent, several functions defined early (for \
example the one that builds an interferometer) are used until the very end, \
so some cells depend on previous ones. A few cells in Part IV time \
computations on purpose; they take up to about a minute each, and the \
absolute times depend on your computer, so only their trends matter."
}], "Text",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell["\<\
Additionally, the story is presented as a continuous sequence, like a movie. \
I have added a few headings to help with transitions from one topic to \
another, but I have avoided breaking the narrative into rigid sections. \
Sometimes a feature is introduced and used before we explain why it applies. \
This is intentional, because the ability to apply an idea often matters more \
than following an abstract proof first. Overall, the rhythm is: concept, then \
computation, then interpretation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell["\<\
Inevitably, some of the code will look complicated at first. My suggestion is \
to focus on the output and its meaning before worrying about every detail of \
the input code. Once you understand what a piece of code is doing \
conceptually, go back and unpack how it is written.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],

Cell["\<\
Remember that you are not locked into the code as given. You can (and should) \
modify it, try your own variations (other angles, other interferometers, more \
photons), and run your own numerical experiments.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "If you have any suggestions or questions, please reach out to us at ",
 ButtonBox["quantum@wolfram.com",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["mailto:quantum@wolfram.com"], None}]
}], "Text",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell["Prerequisites and How to Read This", "Subsection",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To follow the computations comfortably you should be at ease with Dirac \
notation, tensor products, and the creation and annihilation operators of a \
harmonic oscillator, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    SqrtBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],
 ". No background in complexity theory is assumed; the few facts we need are \
stated where they appear. The notebook uses QuantumFramework 2.1 or later, \
whose second-quantization sub-package provides the Fock states, the optical \
elements, and a symbolic algebra of ladder operators that needs version 15 of \
the Wolfram Language."
}], "Text",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell["\<\
Parts I through III build the physics, from two photons to a random \
interferometer. Part IV asks how the cost of simulating the photons grows, \
and it is the part where cells take longer to evaluate.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],

Cell["Let's start!", "Text",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["Part I: Two Photons and One Beam Splitter", "Section",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell["\<\
Setting Up: QuantumFramework and Its Second-Quantization Tools\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell["\<\
QuantumFramework keeps its bosonic tools (Fock states, annihilation \
operators, displacement, squeezing, beam splitters, phase shifters) in a \
separate sub-package. Loading the main package alone leaves those names \
undefined, so we load both.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell["\<\
Load QuantumFramework together with its second-quantization sub-package:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`\>\"", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`QuantumFramework`SecondQuantization`\>\"",
   "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],

Cell["Fock States: Photons as Occupation Numbers", "Subsection",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For light, a mode is one way a photon can travel, for example one arm of an \
interferometer. A state of several photons in several modes is specified by \
how many photons occupy each mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 ", which is called a Fock (or occupation-number) state. A computer cannot \
store the infinitely many levels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "0"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " of a mode, so each mode is truncated to a finite number of levels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 ", holding between zero and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " photons. In other words, a Fock state lists how many photons sit in each \
mode, and the truncation fixes the largest number of photons a single mode \
can hold."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Create the two-mode Fock state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 " (one photon in each mode), keeping three levels (zero, one, or two \
photons) in each mode:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"in", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"in", "[", "\"\<Formula\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],

Cell["Show the dimensions of this truncated two-mode Fock space:", "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"in", "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So the space has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3", "=", "9"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 " basis states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 ", but only three of them, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2,0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0,2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 ", contain exactly two photons. We will see in a moment why the other six \
can never be populated in this experiment."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QuantumFramework orders these basis states by reading the occupations as \
the digits of a base-",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " number, mode 1 being the most significant digit: the position of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " in the state vector is that number plus one."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell["\<\
Define a function that returns the position of an occupation pattern in the \
state vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "fockIndex", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
   RowBox[{"occ_List", ",", " ", "d_Integer"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FromDigits", "[", 
    RowBox[{"occ", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that the state vector of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 " has its only nonzero entry at that position:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"in", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
   RowBox[{"9", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell["The Beam Splitter: A Two-Mode Unitary That Conserves Photons", \
"Subsection",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A beam splitter is a partially reflecting mirror that mixes two modes. \
QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[CurlyPhi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "d", ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 " represents the unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["exp",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}]], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1", "\[Dagger]"], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " acting on modes 1 and 2, each truncated to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " levels. The mixing angle \[Theta] controls how much light crosses from one \
mode to the other: for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 ", a photon that enters mode 1 stays with amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 " and crosses into mode 2 with amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 ", while a photon that enters mode 2 crosses into mode 1 with amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 ". So a single photon stays in its mode with probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],
 " is the balanced (50:50) beam splitter. The angle \[CurlyPhi] is a relative \
phase between the two paths. There are, of course, different conventions: \
many texts parametrize a beam splitter by its transmissivity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 ", and the balanced splitter is often written with a factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " on the reflected path, which corresponds to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 " here. Nothing below depends on that choice. The option ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " builds each matrix element of the untruncated beam splitter from a \
recurrence and keeps the ones that fit below the cutoff; for symbolic angles \
and small cutoffs like ours, it is faster than exponentiating the truncated \
generator."
}], "Text",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a beam splitter with a symbolic mixing angle \[Theta] (and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 ") acting on modes 1 and 2:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look at the generator of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 ": the term ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],
 " removes a photon from mode 1 and puts it into mode 2, and its partner does \
the reverse. So the generator moves photons between the modes without \
creating or destroying any, which means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],
 " commutes with the total photon number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"], "=", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1", "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "+", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 ". In other words, a beam splitter redirects photons; it never adds or \
removes them."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can check this without any truncation. QuantumFramework's symbolic \
bosonic algebra works with the ladder operators themselves, as noncommuting \
formal symbols obeying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ". ",
 Cell[BoxData["FieldVariables"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 " creates them, and ",
 Cell[BoxData["BosonicNormalOrder"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 " rewrites a product of them with every creation operator to the left of \
every annihilation operator, treating the symbols listed in its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Scalars\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " option as ordinary numbers. The built-in ",
 ButtonBox["Commutator",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Commutator.html"], 
    None}],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", 
   RowBox[{"x", ",", " ", "y"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 " gives the commutator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"x", " ", "**", " ", "y"}], " ", "-", " ", 
   RowBox[{"y", " ", "**", " ", "x"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],
 " of two such products. QuantumFramework displays the annihilation operators \
of our two modes as the formal symbols a and b."
}], "Text",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Create the ladder operators of the two modes, the generator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}]], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1", "\[Dagger]"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 " of the beam splitter, and the total photon number:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fieldVars", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FieldVariables", "[", "\[FormalA]", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FieldVariables", "[", "\[FormalB]", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a1", ",", " ", "a1Dag", ",", " ", "a2", ",", " ", "a2Dag"}], 
    "}"}], " ", "=", " ", "fieldVars"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"generator", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"a1", " ", "**", " ", "a2Dag"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Phi]"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"a1Dag", " ", "**", " ", "a2"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"totalNumber", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"a1Dag", " ", "**", " ", "a1"}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"a2Dag", " ", "**", " ", "a2"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the commutator of the generator with the total photon number:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BosonicNormalOrder", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"generator", ",", " ", "totalNumber"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   "fieldVars", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<Scalars\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell["The truncated operator we built inherits this property.", "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the truncated beam splitter commutes with the truncated total \
photon number:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"a1", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"a2", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"ntot", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"a1", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "a1"}], 
        " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"a2", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
         "a2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"bs", " ", "@", " ", "ntot"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ntot", " ", "@", " ", "bs"}]}], ")"}], 
         "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"9", ",", " ", "9"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is why only the three two-photon states can appear after the beam \
splitter: the input ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],
 " carries two photons, and the photon number is conserved."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Photon-number conservation also means that the beam splitter acts \
separately on the states with zero, one, two, and more photons in total. With \
three levels per mode, the sectors with at most two photons are complete, \
while a state like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 " belongs to a three-photon sector that the truncation cuts short: it has no \
room for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"3,0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 ". The ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Recurrence\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 " construction is unitary on the complete sectors, those with at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " photons, and those are the only ones our photons will visit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the beam splitter is unitary on the six states with at most two \
photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mat", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{"bs", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"sel", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
            RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", 
         " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "<=", " ", "2"}], " ", 
          "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mat", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"sel", ",", " ", "sel"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
        RowBox[{"mat", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"sel", ",", " ", "sel"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Length", "[", "sel", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],

Cell["Hong-Ou-Mandel Interference: Why Two Photons Leave Together", \
"Subsection",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],

Cell["\<\
Now let's send the two photons through the beam splitter, one in each input \
port.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 " through the beam splitter and show the output state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"bs", "[", "in", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Formula\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the photons leave in a superposition of three patterns. The \
amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 ", one photon in each output port, is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 ". It is the sum of two histories that end in the same detection event: both \
photons are transmitted (amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 "), or both photons are reflected (amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 "). Because the photons are identical, nothing in the final state records \
which history happened, so the two amplitudes are added before squaring."
}], "Text",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],

Cell["Compute the norm of the output state:", "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Probability\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],
 " divides the squared amplitudes by their total, so a lost norm never shows \
up in it; that is why we check the norm itself."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell["Compute the probability of each detection pattern:", "Text",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
   "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that these probabilities do not depend on the phase \[CurlyPhi] of the \
beam splitter:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], "[",
        "in", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", 
     RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Phi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
    " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],
 ", one photon in each output, is what a pair of detectors records as a \
coincidence, and its probability depends on \[Theta]. Let's find where it \
vanishes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Find the mixing angles between 0 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 " at which the coincidence amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 " is zero:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Solve", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}], " ", "&&",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Theta]", " ", "<", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}]}], ",", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore, at a balanced beam splitter the two histories cancel exactly, \
and two identical photons that enter through different ports always leave \
through the same port, together. This is the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect, named \
after ",
 ButtonBox["Hong, Ou, and Mandel",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.59.2044"], None}],
 ", whose 1987 experiment used this fourth-order (two-photon) interference to \
measure the time interval between two photons. In short, identical photons \
bunch."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell["Distinguishable Photons: Switching the Interference Off", "Subsection",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The cancellation above needs the two histories to be indistinguishable. \
What happens if the photons carry a label that tells them apart? A natural \
label is polarization. Give every path two polarization modes, horizontal (H) \
and vertical (V), and order the four modes as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],
 ". The photon in path 1 is horizontally polarized, and the photon in path 2 \
is polarized at an angle \[Chi], ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["H", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "+", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["V", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],
 ". At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " the photons are identical; at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],
 " their polarizations are orthogonal, and a measurement of polarization \
would reveal which photon went where. Both photons may end up in the same \
horizontal mode, so each mode again needs three levels."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Prepare one horizontal photon in path 1 and one photon polarized at angle \
\[Chi] in path 2 (modes ordered ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["H", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["1", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox["2", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"inPol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", "3"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],

Cell["\<\
A beam splitter that does not care about polarization, called non-polarizing, \
mixes the two horizontal modes and, identically, the two vertical modes.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],

Cell["\<\
Build the non-polarizing beam splitter as a circuit, one copy acting on the \
horizontal modes and one on the vertical modes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bsPol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",",
       "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
        
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],

Cell["\<\
Send the two photons through the non-polarizing beam splitter:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"outPol", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"bsPol", "[", "inPol", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell["Compute the norm of the output state:", "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"outPol", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Chi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
    " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The detectors count photons in each path but ignore polarization. A \
coincidence is therefore any pattern with exactly one photon in path 1 (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["1", 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["1", 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"]]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],
 ") and exactly one photon in path 2 (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["H", "TI"]]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox["2", 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"]]], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 ")."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the coincidence probability, adding up the probabilities of all \
patterns with one photon in each path (",
 ButtonBox["ComplexExpand",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/ComplexExpand.html"], 
    None}],
 " treats the angles \[Theta] and \[Chi] as real):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->878831761,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ComplexExpand", " ", "@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Total", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"KeySelect", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
        RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"outPol", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
       "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}], " ", "&&",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
           RowBox[{"#", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", "1"}]}], " ", 
        "&"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1048559713,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that the coincidence probability equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->300048012,ExpressionUUID->"7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "4"}], " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Theta]", "]"}], "^", "4"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Chi]", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", "2"}]}]}]}], ",",
    " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Chi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
    " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1962937852,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Look at the two limits. For identical photons (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],
 ") the formula collapses to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],
 ", the Hong-Ou-Mandel result."
}], "Text",
 CellID->588230824,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],
 " the coincidence probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2099309037,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Chi]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->512383039,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For orthogonal polarizations (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],
 ") the formula becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],
 ", which is exactly what two independent classical particles give: both \
transmitted or both reflected, with probabilities multiplied rather than \
amplitudes added. In other words, how far the coincidence probability at the \
balanced splitter falls below the value for distinguishable photons measures \
how indistinguishable the photons are, through the squared overlap ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],
 " of their polarization states."
}], "Text",
 CellID->273308241,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Plot the coincidence probability against the mixing angle \[Theta], for \
photons ranging from identical (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ") to fully distinguishable (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1809098798,ExpressionUUID->"107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Plot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Evaluate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "/.", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Chi]", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "6"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "3"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[Chi] = 0\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Chi] = \[Pi]/6\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[Chi] = \[Pi]/3\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Chi] = \[Pi]/2\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Large"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<mixing angle \[Theta]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<coincidence probability\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Coincidence probability for photons with polarization overlap \
Cos[\[Chi]]\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->156430199,ExpressionUUID->"6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As you can see, the balanced beam splitter (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 ") is where identical and distinguishable photons differ most: the classical \
curve never drops below one half, while the identical photons never arrive in \
coincidence."
}], "Text",
 CellID->724760089,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the coincidence probability at the balanced splitter as a function of \
\[Chi]:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->168408080,ExpressionUUID->"0b990c23-b656-01a6-39a6-a58cc3e3538c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "/.", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Chi]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->811283638,ExpressionUUID->"52243646-2fbd-210e-03db-a8204a487054"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, it falls from one half for orthogonal polarizations to zero \
for identical photons. This drop is the Hong-Ou-Mandel dip. In experiments \
the dip is usually recorded by delaying one photon, which makes the two \
photons distinguishable by their arrival times rather than by their \
polarizations.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->207978548,ExpressionUUID->"1acd7f4d-3da3-7753-4af3-7717b4565db9"],

Cell["Too Few Levels: What Truncation Does to Bunching", "Subsection",
 CellID->437474228,ExpressionUUID->"062d91f0-6326-41c0-2fd2-08ba16d3132a"],

Cell["\<\
Recall that we kept three levels in each mode, because the two photons can \
bunch into one mode. Let's see what happens if we are stingy and keep only \
two levels, enough for zero or one photon per mode.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->874582697,ExpressionUUID->"1ac7f74a-ce09-be58-4afc-ef17ebbd04a2"],

Cell["\<\
Apply the same beam splitter with only two levels per mode, and compute the \
norm of the output state:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->11631581,ExpressionUUID->"6f6ad260-8ee1-565a-1569-d44a2a943ca0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->1933762060,ExpressionUUID->"612fd791-c81e-86f2-10d4-cedae9a8ecd8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With two levels per mode the two-photon sector is no longer complete: the \
bunched components ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2,0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26dca2d1-2715-746d-4ee3-3b9b52a05eb7"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0,2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "296a77cd-8fa3-dd44-5f6a-6e972a57a7ae"],
 " have nowhere to go, so this construction simply drops them and the state \
loses norm; at the balanced splitter nothing at all is left. The default ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MatrixExp\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b853673-18d0-d9fa-19ba-a83d996aabc0"],
 " construction fails differently. It exponentiates the truncated generator, \
which keeps the operator unitary, but in the truncated space ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "1"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "2", "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25b5b884-ef74-61b3-534a-31e18a013399"],
 " can no longer put a second photon into mode 2."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1055776787,ExpressionUUID->"574a2197-51ef-7938-7d49-b8d1679a4802"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Repeat with the default ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<MatrixExp\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e85e9ed-427b-8528-16ba-00b7770fec72"],
 " construction, and show the output state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1859711813,ExpressionUUID->"73b76025-96bb-3fff-214d-798f234f85c5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}], 
  "[", "\"\<Formula\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->1348896709,ExpressionUUID->"31f4c073-8ff6-126f-678b-da3d298360b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the norm is preserved, but the physics is wrong: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "72ff7667-e560-b2c0-2285-68408c1a002a"],
 " is frozen, and the photons pass through untouched for every \[Theta]. In \
other words, a simulation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c9be80e-0554-61c1-24b8-0268ace1332b"],
 " photons needs at least ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "106b7ad8-6378-599b-4069-7382160d2be1"],
 " levels in every mode, because all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e6f7c7a-fa8f-2da1-2615-7627ff3a778b"],
 " photons may bunch into one of them. A truncation that is one level too \
small either leaks probability or silently erases the interference. This \
requirement is what makes the truncated Fock space grow so quickly as photons \
are added."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1427211115,ExpressionUUID->"304452a4-201b-d64c-607c-4b0e51afbc96"],

Cell["\<\
The Permanent Appears: The Coincidence Amplitude of a 2\[Times]2 Matrix\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->2099805207,ExpressionUUID->"6beff1f8-c64a-83a6-1994-e8a5f3fcd18c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Everything a beam splitter does to a single photon fits in a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4b5b9263-9199-4e16-7978-144d202c157c"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "475d7054-346c-a3cc-6d63-6a1ebd1ef116"],
 ", the beam splitter's transfer matrix: its entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]},
     "Bra"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2ef71510-aa09-eca9-568c-8d5dcfbdb6f3"],
 " is the amplitude for a photon that enters mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3343f580-98d5-e31c-6170-ecea1961ce66"],
 " to leave from mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20a7420b-376a-b23f-505d-6455421c0105"],
 " (here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SubscriptBox["1", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6af863a9-1098-c609-1a98-7af3a112ad53"],
 " is one photon in mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "055bc2ad-6b92-a3be-3378-dbf70e24f184"],
 " and none elsewhere)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1402006442,ExpressionUUID->"2b0fb60e-2211-365f-5934-286857a59ca5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that reads the transfer matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]},
     "Bra"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      SubscriptBox["1", 
       StyleBox["k", "TI"]]},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "201a2509-bdd9-2fa1-5039-bd53346c758b"],
 " of an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7085d256-6adc-aa08-20ba-d4100f6ef952"],
 "-mode operator by sending one photon into each mode:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1901179466,ExpressionUUID->"5f932952-49a5-d34f-05a0-c11c6851a195"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "transferMatrix", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"transferMatrix", "[", 
   RowBox[{"op_", ",", " ", "m_Integer", ",", " ", "d_Integer"}], "]"}], " ", 
  ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Transpose", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Map", "[", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"op", "[", 
          RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
         "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
            RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
      " ", "&"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "m", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->210724908,ExpressionUUID->"160f17c4-d31a-fe19-3e34-8ea1e6acc563"],

Cell["Compute the transfer matrix of our beam splitter:", "Text",
 CellID->1992790374,ExpressionUUID->"10beb8bd-bdb6-ee93-4045-31e73440b4f9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"transferMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{"bs", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"w", " ", "//", " ", "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->292747604,ExpressionUUID->"3fdc991b-fead-14b0-65e3-1144fb587e9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, a beam splitter with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3657d2c5-05c0-ac85-5e6c-cbafac7af6ef"],
 " acts on a single photon as an ordinary rotation matrix, whose columns hold \
the amplitudes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0642d375-09f3-9942-2e71-cb3faf87eba8"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0651775d-2bad-791b-2e6f-6f074e584861"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", 
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63b9e3d6-2298-231e-1146-fa9057128e64"],
 " we started from. For two photons, the coincidence amplitude we found above \
adds the two histories ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "11"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "22"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67c13665-f813-2f11-0dfe-a84ef9a6727b"],
 " (both transmitted) and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "12"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "21"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c440104-ea8a-4285-747b-99618f3f10ef"],
 " (both reflected) with the same sign. This combination is the permanent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66c9a615-af45-c085-0ef6-385ecaf192ef"],
 ". The permanent of an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0513e607-0f4c-1e20-3320-f861aaf9650a"],
 " matrix is defined like the determinant, as a sum over all permutations \
\[Sigma] of products ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0371ff35-cd30-cda2-310e-f77ee4ca9788"],
 ", but with every term added with a plus sign: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Perm",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "=", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6833ae6a-6ac5-a2c8-19c0-40340f71f012"],
 ". The Wolfram Language computes it with ",
 ButtonBox["Permanent",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Permanent.html"], None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1553818268,ExpressionUUID->"5f7f2999-1aee-25a5-0504-c0c39e988f8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the permanent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "128c7526-c883-085d-42b4-6c83e9365aa7"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1870754514,ExpressionUUID->"3279c00f-c9e2-8758-6206-da68ef94eda2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", "w", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->1358728755,ExpressionUUID->"50b12ff8-e606-85f7-004e-c6a593b0efdd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that the permanent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "640f47a5-4648-c62d-0c35-5e0f73e2ad77"],
 " is exactly the amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63a48922-0fac-666c-115b-208caa594cb6"],
 " in the output state:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->935019337,ExpressionUUID->"387a9e0d-0234-0e73-6819-1057b7c15559"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", "w", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"psi", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
     "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->642744358,ExpressionUUID->"3f64ca0d-9927-5f44-651b-ec5718d225ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two identical fermions in the same situation pick up a minus sign when \
their histories are exchanged, so their coincidence amplitude is the \
determinant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "11"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "22"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "12"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], "21"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "399d1ff3-4632-be92-6fa2-96bd73c404f8"],
 " instead of the permanent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1478372881,ExpressionUUID->"1170384d-2f38-2c50-470f-b2174acd76ba"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the determinant of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ce33075-6d34-44a7-1490-aa3f04c12e8d"],
 ", the corresponding amplitude for two identical fermions:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->124263719,ExpressionUUID->"54e2b6d5-0ba4-5b19-7c91-2f9fae512663"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Det", "[", "w", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->1310926461,ExpressionUUID->"6334ac9c-43f1-85c0-12cb-45c67585ef2a"],

Cell["\<\
This means that two identical fermions always leave through different ports, \
the exact opposite of the bunching bosons: the exchange sign turns the \
destructive interference into constructive interference. We will return to \
this contrast at the very end, because the difference between a permanent and \
a determinant is also the difference between a hard and an easy computation.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1124211690,ExpressionUUID->"74397683-04f4-1d4d-1dc7-6fedac816797"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For distinguishable photons, the probabilities of the two histories add \
instead of the amplitudes, which amounts to the permanent of the matrix of \
single-photon probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "735e49d5-32a1-4a48-2166-609f47541892"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1335749844,ExpressionUUID->"335d55a2-cf9b-493d-6163-4c0fea2e1807"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the permanent of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bfbbd45-edb8-1b0b-6998-352e844d6651"],
 ", the coincidence probability for distinguishable photons:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->793802945,ExpressionUUID->"045023ab-c37d-b770-2c6f-baf4f6091a5a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->631769182,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that it equals the coincidence probability of the polarization model \
at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1873681340,ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"coincidence", " ", "/.", " ", 
      RowBox[{"\[Chi]", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->1468251080,ExpressionUUID->"167ebcf0-2b32-2a61-3e05-35ba4ec7794b"],

Cell["\<\
Before we move on, let us summarize the most important points we have learned \
so far:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1989234463,ExpressionUUID->"15eb24b6-b946-3a65-43e8-bdf038f0894f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A Fock state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27d2a24c-1e84-19ee-4de1-44169b316b34"],
 " lists the photons in each mode, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"n1", ",", " ", "n2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], ",", " ", "d"}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "285985c7-a1c8-13eb-5866-1ca0d07d6131"],
 " keeps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57868ed1-450c-c474-7dbd-279b6cbeaf5e"],
 " levels per mode."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1607696641,ExpressionUUID->"0c5e608e-35dc-f74f-3466-79e8bc6edd95"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A beam splitter commutes with the total photon number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1a1e4090-3303-05ed-4a26-59da46b66f37"],
 ", in the untruncated algebra and in the truncated space, so it only \
redistributes photons, and it is unitary on every photon-number sector that \
the truncation holds completely."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1817342824,ExpressionUUID->"10256af3-3972-af7a-41da-83bdb804f240"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "457602f1-d86e-ac86-730d-9bbad918f6ec"],
 " the coincidence amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "499f95c1-a958-6c18-7fa4-0caac8ed3762"],
 ", which vanishes at the balanced splitter: identical photons leave together \
(the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect)."
}], "Item",
 CellID->530774412,ExpressionUUID->"0f1e874b-6d22-b8ab-3525-1f1504d40af1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With a polarization overlap ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c02104f-9807-e6c4-3431-8a2919b3cc2e"],
 ", the coincidence probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6f909018-5ea1-6a32-15af-0a425b543918"],
 ", which interpolates between identical and distinguishable photons; at the \
balanced splitter it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Chi]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f4595f3-090a-1216-557a-0cbda8bf617c"],
 ", the Hong-Ou-Mandel dip."
}], "Item",
 CellID->599957810,ExpressionUUID->"06385f5e-e9d4-4e6c-2fd8-571b886114b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A simulation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25d2fb85-296f-82e5-53e1-f2ef481bd0cf"],
 " photons needs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b9a140e-d97a-4136-69b9-8e6bd80f101c"],
 " levels per mode; fewer levels either lose probability or erase the \
interference."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1899946997,ExpressionUUID->"4f9438da-b80f-a114-75ab-b18439bbf07e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coincidence amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Perm",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7281c19b-2602-dcd4-22be-d8c553b4a63e"],
 " of the transfer matrix; for fermions it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["det",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3c8746fc-db76-c487-64bd-5fb9de00aeed"],
 ", and for distinguishable photons the coincidence probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Perm",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       StyleBox["W", "TI"]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11f0f87a-e6f0-91cd-478f-f227928ae317"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1051619128,ExpressionUUID->"473164ce-b547-c1f4-6ecf-7da83cf393de"],

Cell["Part II: Three Photons in a Three-Mode Interferometer", "Section",
 CellID->1921351195,ExpressionUUID->"12c4fc3b-e00c-2bba-42fb-f66491b97980"],

Cell["\<\
Any Interferometer Is a Mesh of Beam Splitters: The Reck Decomposition\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1207491739,ExpressionUUID->"1d7e6892-18cd-6f45-4b05-81dc997835af"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A passive linear-optical network with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "325c8f47-cd85-89da-6263-2720e431db20"],
 " modes (mirrors, beam splitters, phase shifters, no photons created and no \
light lost) acts on a single photon as an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fcea2e-12ab-c026-7183-0388a75f930c"],
 " unitary matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b416c07-c3d3-bf4f-097e-8660f6670595"],
 ". The remarkable converse, given by ",
 ButtonBox["Reck, Zeilinger, Bernstein, and Bertani in 1994",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.73.58"], None}],
 " as a recursive algorithm, is that every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5add4728-e92e-eff1-0ae3-5f7588d8b5db"],
 " unitary factorizes into a sequence of two-mode beam-splitter \
transformations, so any interferometer can be built in the laboratory. We \
will build such a factorization ourselves, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "621761a3-d300-b412-122d-780ce6ba1f78"],
 " single-mode phase shifters followed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b08d465-1dcc-fb87-0937-ce4f947ec9ed"],
 " beam splitters, in the order the light meets them. Let's first count \
degrees of freedom to see why that many is the right number. A unitary in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d3ffb2e-09a8-fc78-24c4-f288a842c742"],
 " carries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4139b36b-52b1-2977-70c6-2b356744785d"],
 " real parameters. Each beam splitter carries two (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "494d6e39-7750-b6eb-7f72-806302ea1c31"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39b01e29-d171-5c92-6f4f-9072e00426f8"],
 "), which gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f6d713e-2461-11c8-7513-69784d146312"],
 ", and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14ad582f-66ff-93eb-3c53-5189128be131"],
 " phase shifters add the remaining ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f7ea056-2d28-85ec-7505-3a1044c2ef36"],
 ". So the count matches exactly. In other words, beam splitters and phase \
shifters are all we ever need."
}], "Text",
 CellID->216741342,ExpressionUUID->"16b00368-b832-202d-3e4f-9b3239c77377"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "First we need the transfer matrix of a QuantumFramework beam splitter \
placed on modes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06d00634-a672-f252-2eef-9871d304c0b8"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05feeeaf-4f58-f7b7-3385-07096ad2dd9d"],
 " of an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "583a98af-415b-100e-09d9-110970ee6354"],
 "-mode network. With the phase \[CurlyPhi] restored, it is the identity \
except for the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07beae85-a317-6bf9-2d45-47eed6a239c3"],
 " block ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
     {
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["cos",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
      RowBox[{"-", 
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]}]], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]},
     {
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"i", "\[Phi]"}], "TI"]], 
       StyleBox["sin",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["cos",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]}
    }], ")"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "503c05d1-55e8-8c5e-01c3-9c9b6382d6a4"],
 " on rows and columns ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60049622-f570-0e0e-103b-0f8ffc055554"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40ea559d-da93-7842-70ea-4cc6df264aa8"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2096934290,ExpressionUUID->"23ccc6ee-92c0-e596-51f3-dfc8277acffc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "114d8d02-b276-9c05-4772-256fc700e76f"],
 " block of a beam splitter with angles \[Theta] and \[CurlyPhi]:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1367217003,ExpressionUUID->"2dc22b63-32d1-862f-5bf1-c34d4765ed75"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "bsBlock", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"t_", ",", " ", "f_"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "f"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
        RowBox[{"I", " ", "f"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "t", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "t", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->1372538143,ExpressionUUID->"36ea7e2c-072a-2221-5eea-7076b2df710b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that this block is the transfer matrix that QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData["BeamSplitterOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b23761c-2477-64e8-0ad1-68464d024e32"],
 " produces, for symbolic \[Theta] and \[CurlyPhi]:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->485911656,ExpressionUUID->"73216bcf-7cf1-61ac-22de-82a9748433f6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    
    RowBox[{"transferMatrix", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "2", ",", 
        " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",",
       " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Phi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
    " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[35]:= ",
 CellID->181917407,ExpressionUUID->"69fa63e8-c0ca-4913-1f9a-7ab5f17f1879"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now the decomposition itself. Take the unitary ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "409bca18-cbd6-e54d-70b8-ec45ee60cf97"],
 " and look at two neighboring rows ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10b62b5f-1d3f-f012-404d-c31994cbc378"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79984792-c453-565a-2fb8-5edfede63ca0"],
 " of column ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d45428e-8fa1-6801-4b7b-5be82a543b6b"],
 ", with entries ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], "-", "1"}], ",", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "604bb87d-3174-a116-1048-32274006f07c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "j"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "763191a2-6f8b-197a-1fce-080c0a3e6840"],
 ". A beam splitter on modes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "635fdfdb-2856-deda-1164-d68549e0a420"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f6eb37a-d9e9-6713-3515-2b27df9c4a79"],
 " mixes only these two rows. Multiplying them from the left by the inverse \
of the block with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["tan",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["b", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "/", GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox["a", "TI"]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8469dd-bfc7-2a7a-04bb-80873a727940"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["arg",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "*"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "182ee0c1-720e-fc83-49d5-f9ab07b8c6e9"],
 ", the phase of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3921e4bb-f5e4-3596-68de-fde483969ffc"],
 " relative to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["a", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13db9173-5387-1c16-41f8-093d6632677c"],
 ", turns the entry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6804c0ab-fd16-b7db-183b-d9f4f4a01d21"],
 " into zero. Sweeping column by column, from the bottom row upward, zeros \
every entry below the diagonal after ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77076ae4-09e5-8344-1d3c-83ceaf91d1ae"],
 " steps. What remains is an upper-triangular unitary matrix, and an \
upper-triangular unitary matrix is diagonal: a list of phases ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4289b0c6-8043-1b93-72b6-29a031f669f9"],
 ". Writing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "070f3e08-556d-9d60-2d34-b0525c19e44a"],
 " for the transfer matrix of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d593b15-c37a-9c59-1b66-b35ef60ce6a3"],
 "-th beam splitter of the sweep and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4140e475-1e41-1f16-777f-fe3f9bf4627c"],
 " for their number, this means ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "\[Ellipsis]", 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "1", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67f13035-938c-831a-0d8e-aa7f263eee60"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "1"], "\[Ellipsis]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["D", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "16b44e14-0404-e868-3e4c-605eadb6bab2"],
 ": in the laboratory, the light first meets the phase shifters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["D", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70bc3c38-1a7f-2cd8-2043-b6629f0a7622"],
 " and then the beam splitters in reverse order. This is essentially a QR \
decomposition by Givens rotations, carried out with physical beam splitters."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1906087345,ExpressionUUID->"7e10bd94-ae42-3b4d-262f-34d1cbf48997"],

Cell["\<\
Define one nulling step, which records the beam-splitter angles it used and \
updates the two rows it mixes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->354048744,ExpressionUUID->"5fdf5ac0-01aa-1326-05e5-53aab05f7e0c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "nullingStep", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nullingStep", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"i_", ",", " ", "j_"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
      ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "j"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
    "  ", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"angles", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"If", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"PossibleZeroQ", "[", "b", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"ArcTan", "[", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "a", "]"}], ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "b", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"Arg", "[", 
              RowBox[{"b", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "a", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
           "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sow", "[", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"angles", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "i"}], "}"}]}], 
         "}"}], "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
        RowBox[{"w", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "i"}], "}"}], " ", "->",
            " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", "angles", "]"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"w", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"i", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "i"}], "}"}], 
              "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[36]:= ",
 CellID->786710823,ExpressionUUID->"013c2307-fb8b-27c7-30c3-bb60fe3f8d2d"],

Cell["\<\
Define the decomposition, which folds the nulling steps over the entries \
below the diagonal, column by column and from the bottom up, and returns the \
remaining diagonal together with the recorded beam splitters:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1859374462,ExpressionUUID->"4b734859-75e7-efa6-7901-62030393b58c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "reckDecomposition", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"reckDecomposition", "[", 
   RowBox[{"u_", "?", "SquareMatrixQ"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Length", "[", "u", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Reap", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
      RowBox[{"nullingStep", ",", " ", "u", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Catenate", " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "j"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"m", " ", "-", " ", "1"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"i", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"j", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[37]:= ",
 CellID->544914423,ExpressionUUID->"4ae31c17-eefa-a706-7a90-96508a8c0a6c"],

Cell["\<\
Define a function that tabulates recorded beam splitters by their angles and \
the pair of modes each one acts on:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1088734259,ExpressionUUID->"00844d77-2817-3ec6-30bc-653149a3842c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "splitterTable", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"splitterTable", "[", "splitters_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Append", " ", "@@@", " ", "splitters"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<\[Theta]\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<\[Phi]\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<modes\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[38]:= ",
 CellID->476175344,ExpressionUUID->"20b97f64-b973-0c8a-5047-774e380656d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's test it on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04469009-6b02-dcc3-2c7d-0a530eb4a629"],
 " discrete Fourier matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"r", "s"}], "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["s", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "/", 
   SqrtBox["3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4e35d333-5bd5-ef26-77ca-cb7d5e61b20c"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[Pi]", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], "/", "3"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5547dfb6-0e84-e145-037c-d6f0ab36b3af"],
 ", which the Wolfram Language provides as ",
 ButtonBox["FourierMatrix",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/FourierMatrix.html"], 
    None}],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->201272189,ExpressionUUID->"12b61bfc-9cd7-eca9-424d-92a61563b6f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Decompose the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "451364b5-819d-fb99-7321-7dff3029c9e3"],
 " Fourier matrix and show the diagonal of phases that remains:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->320292756,ExpressionUUID->"13b49e24-0fb7-4441-414b-178eaa422eab"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"fourierDiagonal", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "fourierSplitters", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"reckDecomposition", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", "fourierDiagonal", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "MatrixForm"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[39]:= ",
 CellID->1146801282,ExpressionUUID->"445bf28f-7a5a-ecd1-6c78-ebe97fecb63b"],

Cell["\<\
Show the angles \[Theta] and \[CurlyPhi] and the mode pairs of the three beam \
splitters:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->41202278,ExpressionUUID->"089aa42d-ce49-3603-38b9-3e76ebfd9d69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"splitterTable", "[", "fourierSplitters", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[40]:= ",
 CellID->1124146653,ExpressionUUID->"48fccab3-b886-a0f7-7883-e3fd3930f2dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, three beam splitters are enough, with exact angles. The \
decomposition uses nothing but algebra, so it also accepts symbolic entries; \
let's try it on a single beam splitter with symbolic angles. The nulling step \
returns mixing angles between 0 and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cdaad60-2181-5e26-34f9-454a5034250c"],
 " and phases between ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "542cff75-84e0-b601-7dd3-f73f2c9a1d6b"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00dd9d4d-f7ec-565f-30e2-151681993ca5"],
 ", so we give the symbolic angles those ranges."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1232284935,ExpressionUUID->"0d66b502-775d-ec4c-3b1d-2d6c02e9b696"],

Cell["\<\
Decompose the transfer matrix of a beam splitter with symbolic angles \
\[Alpha] and \[Beta], and show the beam splitter it records:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2082395230,ExpressionUUID->"3a3bfee8-9a0e-4a4b-6bd8-f7b21fbb1891"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"symbolicDiagonal", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "symbolicSplitters", "}"}]}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"reckDecomposition", "[", 
      RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"0", " ", "<", " ", "\[Alpha]", " ", "<", " ", 
       RowBox[{"\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]}], " ", "&&", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "\[Pi]"}], " ", "<", " ", "\[Beta]", " ", "<", " ", 
       "\[Pi]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"splitterTable", "[", "symbolicSplitters", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[41]:= ",
 CellID->2045146513,ExpressionUUID->"333832e2-8bec-4128-62c7-abcc2d991072"],

Cell["Verify that no phases are left over:", "Text",
 CellID->25123057,ExpressionUUID->"78cf51d6-d7cd-4672-28f5-4893e2782d58"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"symbolicDiagonal", " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[42]:= ",
 CellID->371825621,ExpressionUUID->"1d9e3d6f-99f1-7c1e-4ba5-b5491f844764"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the decomposition returns exactly the beam splitter we \
started from. A phase shifter on mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "710db4a8-d877-0db2-2732-2df5d9025798"],
 " is QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"PhaseShiftOperator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", " ", "d", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "p", "}"}]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71e12f72-3ad4-a92f-279e-c73cbf66f875"],
 ", the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["p", "TI"]]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06ea8612-dd18-b4f0-2ee9-185fd4921eda"],
 ", which multiplies a photon in mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b02f270-2101-5c3d-3931-f43a50b42707"],
 " by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"i", "\[Alpha]"}], "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1868bf-f524-2aaf-5b27-81f8fcd178f5"],
 ". So we can now turn the decomposition into a QuantumFramework circuit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1439628390,ExpressionUUID->"669caa83-24d6-d7e9-0ea3-43ed4d60bd33"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that turns any unitary into a QuantumFramework circuit of \
phase shifters followed by beam splitters, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5ae50fd0-6d1f-8fa4-0a9a-a69a04abd58e"],
 " levels in every mode:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->497245720,ExpressionUUID->"66e7a4a8-d710-64fe-0e9c-3df5e2a54ec4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "interferometer", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"u_", "?", "UnitaryMatrixQ"}], ",", " ", "d_Integer", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"opts", " ", ":", " ", 
     RowBox[{"OptionsPattern", "[", "BeamSplitterOperator", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], 
  " ", ":=", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"r", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"reckDecomposition", "[", "u", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Join", "[", "\n", "    ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"PhaseShiftOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", "d", ",", " ", "#2"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], ",",
          " ", 
         RowBox[{"Arg", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Diagonal", " ", "@", " ", 
           RowBox[{"First", "[", "r", "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", "d", ",", " ", "#2", ",", " ", "opts"}], 
          "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Catenate", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Last", "[", "r", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[43]:= ",
 CellID->1090726268,ExpressionUUID->"3e73fafe-05d0-7203-6600-f3b8ac654169"],

Cell["The Fourier Tritter: Six Dark Outputs", "Subsection",
 CellID->2124519200,ExpressionUUID->"7fb7b09a-ac3b-ef52-254c-29c7c5cfb5b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12c044c4-b778-74e1-42f0-5da1c20d5ecb"],
 " Fourier matrix describes a symmetric three-port beam splitter, often \
called a tritter: a single photon entering any port leaves through each of \
the three ports with probability one third. We will send three photons into \
it, one per port, so each mode needs four levels."
}], "Text",
 CellID->617350884,ExpressionUUID->"3d9aa029-60a8-273a-6bb9-3a7311428a00"],

Cell["\<\
Build the Fourier tritter with four levels per mode and draw its circuit:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1357963930,ExpressionUUID->"64adc082-4122-deff-0c52-d9ec70d4a4c5"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tritter", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"tritter", "[", "\"\<Diagram\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[44]:= ",
 CellID->1626918454,ExpressionUUID->"7e451771-8a55-ceec-267a-8f3b2fe19436"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the circuit acts on a single photon exactly as the Fourier matrix \
(two levels per mode are enough to read the transfer matrix):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->675379980,ExpressionUUID->"4670f053-f537-0b3f-6e0f-ea1cfcc25605"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"transferMatrix", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", "3", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[45]:= ",
 CellID->1331866192,ExpressionUUID->"330aabc0-bdd5-22a3-6109-42aa34607089"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three photons can be arranged in three modes in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"3", "+", "3", "-", "1"}], "3"},
    "Binomial"], "=", "10"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38c8cb12-19a5-fbf9-68f7-e35c9851c9c3"],
 " ways, from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"3,0,0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70d705b8-410a-1477-20ec-9ce270bf7f5d"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "737c509e-bc52-eefb-2104-49d835e4b4c1"],
 ". For distinguishable photons each photon would pick its exit port \
independently, and every one of these patterns would occur. Let's see what \
identical photons do."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1391655620,ExpressionUUID->"01a44b6b-c85f-9e0e-375c-6334e9ebe554"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send one photon into each mode, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "10bcaec6-cc03-bcfd-4043-47a3e5b706c7"],
 ", and compute the probabilities of the detection patterns that occur:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->861714746,ExpressionUUID->"25120901-cfbc-a8e6-5321-a16aea4efacc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tritterOut", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"tritter", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "4"}], 
     "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"tritterProbabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"tritterOut", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[46]:= ",
 CellID->1192942815,ExpressionUUID->"3ee7491f-72c3-8814-669d-61590777db7e"],

Cell["Verify that the output state is normalized:", "Text",
 CellID->556077107,ExpressionUUID->"67860241-8011-89c8-0dbd-a42b31a5db12"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tritterOut", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "1"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[47]:= ",
 CellID->15883883,ExpressionUUID->"1318f44b-7a0d-b86f-4127-ee157fb90ab5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Have you noticed something interesting? Only four of the ten patterns ever \
occur: either all three photons leave together through one port, or they \
leave one per port. The six patterns with exactly two photons in one port are \
completely dark, for any number of repetitions of the experiment. This is a \
many-photon generalization of the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect, the \
zero-transmission (or suppression) law of ",
 ButtonBox["Tichy and collaborators (2010)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1002.5038"], None}],
 ": when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "221ecbfd-1ed7-d323-5225-e2a79b63be09"],
 " photons enter the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f067a83-888f-4db3-653e-73ed293a1799"],
 " ports of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287fc527-5526-9e30-5804-dc815cd0e51a"],
 "-mode Fourier interferometer, one per port, every output pattern for which \
the sum of the output mode labels of all the photons, counted from 0, is not \
a multiple of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2207e002-80f7-0285-523c-fa6c308250ef"],
 " is exactly dark. The law gives a sufficient condition; as its authors \
note, the converse does not hold in general, so a pattern that passes the \
test can still be dark. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "440467ae-8db5-79b4-6c3c-7e0824404b9e"],
 " the coincidence pattern has labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"0", "+", "1", "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "141585f4-d1c1-5bbd-3c2a-1cb1e0742987"],
 ", which is odd, and we recover the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect."
}], "Text",
 CellID->308842859,ExpressionUUID->"3d27d006-86b8-9131-64dc-ca603332e01b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that the coincidence amplitude of two photons in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e44340b-ef5c-51d5-667b-ae548ae9233f"],
 " Fourier matrix, which is a balanced beam splitter up to phases, is zero:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1108042358,ExpressionUUID->"321034f4-436e-dcec-622f-adbe7618a636"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[48]:= ",
 CellID->1009200201,ExpressionUUID->"1287d3f9-6500-de4e-42bc-caa30cbaa494"],

Cell["\<\
Now let's test the law on every pattern of our three photons.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->752465254,ExpressionUUID->"3035d7f6-28ea-dcd5-61ca-ceb0489ca63f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The occupation lists of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "087f5f2f-6486-1b59-3805-56890d3369a3"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ddf1aac-cdaa-cd7e-2be4-9309e45c9444"],
 " modes are the solutions of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "1"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b41c4a9-15e8-1804-597e-ddf3a39d6b6e"],
 " in nonnegative integers, which ",
 ButtonBox["FrobeniusSolve",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/FrobeniusSolve.html"], 
    None}],
 " finds."
}], "Text",
 CellID->891183881,ExpressionUUID->"13ecd9ee-6506-67bb-4193-d0c80cb34d81"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that lists all ways of placing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6724c974-bdf1-27a5-0edb-e13e3b858d8f"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2b52875c-0948-9ae8-5961-1f06a8e2e832"],
 " modes, as occupation lists:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->741634648,ExpressionUUID->"53412643-5a68-df00-017e-b82d5f02a26a"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "photonPatterns", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "m_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"ReverseSort", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrobeniusSolve", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
    "]"}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[49]:= ",
 CellID->359589406,ExpressionUUID->"696f5b1d-d56b-3a26-1f15-5346dc1f890c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that there are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0eb02373-2484-618c-364f-bb3d4d3133d6"],
 " patterns for three photons in three modes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->533832725,ExpressionUUID->"640353f1-ff8e-e9b3-0c31-4abafa38bb99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "3", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[50]:= ",
 CellID->739917449,ExpressionUUID->"37161f66-4600-a3a8-5d2d-974073baf1f2"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that, for three photons, the law accounts for every dark pattern: a \
pattern is dark exactly when the sum of its photons' mode labels (counted \
from 0) is not a multiple of 3:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->473762610,ExpressionUUID->"2e44757e-c407-f813-567c-6d3bedb3cb79"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PossibleZeroQ", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tritterProbabilities", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Key", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "===",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"!", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Divisible", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], ",", " ",
         "3"}], "]"}]}]}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[51]:= ",
 CellID->1751712322,ExpressionUUID->"07a61755-6475-fbf7-2d5d-8f1f0d01c9dd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "539b0e4e-9e5a-5525-01b8-a0281bef3c0f"],
 " photons need ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cd82739-42e3-b7ed-44e7-bf6376971d37"],
 " levels in every mode. With three photons we can now see what one level too \
few does to a suppression law."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1390140890,ExpressionUUID->"0971a20b-7913-467e-3f0e-445578a62d44"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09df342d-d743-5809-3fe4-ae76e2f62b53"],
 " through the tritter built with three levels per mode and the default \
construction, and compute the probabilities of the patterns that occur:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1031105928,ExpressionUUID->"0a0cc1e9-e2ca-26d9-3a33-d8b2977c8c23"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
  RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
       "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[52]:= ",
 CellID->1410588720,ExpressionUUID->"21fdaace-430e-f3f9-5782-43a876b8c1c3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the patterns with two photons in one port, which the law \
forbids, now carry most of the probability, and the probability of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],
 " drops below its value of one third."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1051974278,ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the squared norm of the output state when the tritter is built with \
the recurrence construction instead:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1989924844,ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
      "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[53]:= ",
 CellID->695529426,ExpressionUUID->"62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],

Cell["\<\
So with one level too few, the default construction invents detection events \
that the law forbids, and the recurrence construction loses more than half of \
the probability.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->767788723,ExpressionUUID->"34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],

Cell["Every Probability Is a Permanent", "Subsection",
 CellID->494419947,ExpressionUUID->"166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall that the coincidence amplitude of two photons was the permanent of \
their transfer matrix. The same holds for any number of photons. For ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 " photons entering with occupations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], "1"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],
 " and leaving with occupations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], "1"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["m", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 ", build the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],
 " by taking row ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"],
 " of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 " as many times as there are photons leaving mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 ", and column ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 " as many times as there are photons entering mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 ". Then the amplitude is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]},
     "Bra"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]},
     "Ket"]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Perm",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
        StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], "/", 
     SqrtBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"],
          LimitsPositioning->False], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       RowBox[{
        UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"],
         LimitsPositioning->False], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "!"}]}]}]]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],
 ", and for distinguishable photons the probability is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Perm",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],
 ". In words: every way of routing the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],
 " photons to the detected modes contributes one product of single-photon \
amplitudes, and identical photons add all these contributions before squaring."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1581507689,ExpressionUUID->"1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],

Cell["\<\
Define the row (or column) list of an occupation pattern, and the two \
probabilities:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2120100675,ExpressionUUID->"19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
  RowBox[{
  "modeList", ",", " ", "bosonProbability", ",", " ", 
   "distinguishableProbability"}], "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "occ_List", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Catenate", " ", "@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}], ",", " ", "#1"}], "]"}], " ", 
      "&"}], ",", " ", "occ"}], "]"}]}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
      RowBox[{"w", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^",
     "2"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"s", "!"}], ")"}]}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"t", "!"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "s_", ",", " ", "t_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{"w", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "t", "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", 
     "2"}], "]"}], "/", 
   RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"t", "!"}], ")"}]}]}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[54]:= ",
 CellID->950326543,ExpressionUUID->"6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For distinguishable photons, each photon picks its exit on its own: the \
history in which photon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],
 " leaves through port ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["k", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],
 ", for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],
 ", has probability ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
         StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 ", and the histories that end in the same pattern add up."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1689126594,ExpressionUUID->"2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify, for a general complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"3", "\[Times]", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],
 " matrix, that adding up these histories pattern by pattern gives the \
formula for distinguishable photons:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1490757098,ExpressionUUID->"6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"wGeneral", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalW]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"byPattern", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"GroupBy", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Counts", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", 
          "&"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"MapIndexed", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                   RowBox[{"wGeneral", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"[", 
                    RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", 
                    RowBox[{"First", "[", "#2", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], 
                  "^", "2"}], " ", "&"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", 
             "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"byPattern", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
            RowBox[{"wGeneral", ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
             "#"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ", "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[55]:= ",
 CellID->148290444,ExpressionUUID->"7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that every tritter probability computed in Fock space by \
QuantumFramework equals the permanent formula:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1707667820,ExpressionUUID->"5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
       RowBox[{"tritterProbabilities", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Key", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "#"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[56]:= ",
 CellID->933399197,ExpressionUUID->"34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The permanent formula holds for every interferometer, not only for the \
Fourier one. Take a mesh of three beam splitters with symbolic angles on \
three modes. The transfer matrix of each splitter is the identity with its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],
 " block placed on its two modes, and the light meets the first splitter \
first, so the mesh has the transfer matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "3"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "2"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "1"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->955179929,ExpressionUUID->"29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that QuantumFramework's Fock-space amplitudes for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47740231-7fc8-4299-6d0b-a47b7a7d10e3"],
 " through this symbolic mesh are the permanents of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1af52337-5e42-c8c3-4a8a-bb715bf49a29"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->775067320,ExpressionUUID->"2fdb82dc-2353-e9b3-55f8-1b8656e7bb99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"splitters", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Theta]1", ",", " ", "\[Phi]1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Theta]2", ",", " ", "\[Phi]2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Theta]3", ",", " ", "\[Phi]3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"out", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"QuantumCircuitOperator", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"BeamSplitterOperator", "[", 
              RowBox[{"#1", ",", " ", "4", ",", " ", "#2", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Recurrence\>\""}]}], 
              "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", "splitters"}], "]"}], "[", 
          RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
       "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Dot", " ", "@@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Reverse", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"Thread", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Tuples", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"#2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", "#1", "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}],
             " ", "&"}], " ", "@@@", " ", "splitters"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
      "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"out", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
              RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "-", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
             RowBox[{"w", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"{", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"#", "!"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ",
          "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[57]:= ",
 CellID->72268088,ExpressionUUID->"5782d92f-a790-094a-7db1-d088d2255b90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The formula also covers inputs with more than one photon in a mode, through \
the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["s", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05d48452-325d-a277-33eb-1e1c47e9f15d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->546416532,ExpressionUUID->"087ffcf6-194e-431e-3804-f5b098fb2e64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Send ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2,1,0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "615fadf7-df9a-5675-1764-44b0da2f3d5f"],
 ", two photons into the first port and one into the second, through the \
tritter and compute the probabilities of the patterns that occur:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2117784656,ExpressionUUID->"5de452e3-5fd7-a751-0b9c-4bcd5a630dbb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"probabilities210", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
   RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"tritter", "[", 
       RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "4"}],
         "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[58]:= ",
 CellID->853117843,ExpressionUUID->"2d0df906-1ebb-1081-5b32-f1609b4e62eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that every one of these probabilities equals the permanent formula \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519a4e0d-3467-bfb9-07ba-6057bd130583"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->623836386,ExpressionUUID->"3a891815-8c00-cf41-6ab6-925f25ba95ab"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
       RowBox[{"probabilities210", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Key", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", "0"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
      " ", 
      RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", "#"}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[59]:= ",
 CellID->564394165,ExpressionUUID->"0dbacffa-31b0-43f6-3b59-e6a4404511dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, this input spreads evenly over nine patterns and leaves ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "196a859c-b643-c1b3-4f69-1cd9c3f79399"],
 " dark, a dark pattern about which the law for one photon per port says \
nothing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2048244887,ExpressionUUID->"48c8a383-1e42-ef31-78f7-3aed9bf4b21b"],

Cell["\<\
Compare identical photons with distinguishable photons, pattern by pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432457359,ExpressionUUID->"50735439-04fd-dee7-0001-4e63ac89a4cd"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", "\n", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          "#"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
          "#"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
      RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuditName", " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<bosons\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<distinguishable\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[60]:= ",
 CellID->200346680,ExpressionUUID->"3597ba8d-914b-928f-63ac-33d720ffe0d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As you may have noticed, distinguishable photons populate all ten patterns, \
and together the six patterns with two photons in one port carry most of \
their probability. Identical photons empty exactly those patterns and move \
their weight to the fully bunched patterns and to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "056fda38-a5bc-2884-3314-dc65cc497aee"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->447384324,ExpressionUUID->"383c4a9f-130c-f8c1-69c4-63d9a6beca2b"],

Cell["\<\
With the permanent formula we can also test the suppression law for more \
photons, without building any Fock space. Recall that the law only guarantees \
darkness; it does not promise that every pattern it allows is bright.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1438124241,ExpressionUUID->"7b649e79-a2e1-7610-291b-1022d6945d7a"],

Cell["\<\
Find the patterns of six photons in the six-mode Fourier interferometer that \
are dark although the law allows them:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2000382747,ExpressionUUID->"09cb884c-5fc8-b209-3fc8-22165a620153"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
    RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Divisible", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], ",", " ", 
       "6"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PossibleZeroQ", "[", 
      RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"FourierMatrix", "[", "6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "]"}]}],
     " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[61]:= ",
 CellID->902867877,ExpressionUUID->"376c6589-bcca-29e8-5d14-7cd3357f7b32"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, at six photons interference darkens more patterns than the \
law predicts. The law is a sufficient condition for darkness, not a necessary \
one.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1315202099,ExpressionUUID->"667bb688-7420-22c7-0e18-2fd27dd5702d"],

Cell["\<\
Before we move on, let us summarize the most important points we have learned \
so far:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->376763343,ExpressionUUID->"72002252-da4c-5210-223f-c41fdff9217a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "084561a7-5440-aaee-387b-78015dfaf834"],
 "-mode interferometer is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "721e71e5-9ca7-ded5-2226-68cf1553a43f"],
 " beam splitters and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0a84e7eb-55e0-1894-3abb-feb563956afe"],
 " phase shifters, which matches the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3261920b-7b77-02d6-621e-14557e02503c"],
 " real parameters of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebe3b2c-9c8f-bd2d-7645-b376153b0477"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->126027414,ExpressionUUID->"7d6a0058-fb4a-caff-2b69-9a05fefc98c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
   RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "d"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "41d92934-9aba-8299-77e6-c17e1f4cd0e3"],
 " builds that mesh from QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData["BeamSplitterOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5cc23ff5-bf0f-f019-04f1-b6bf3abbc363"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["PhaseShiftOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29880975-91f0-008f-5fb7-a13f278552d5"],
 ", and its transfer matrix reproduces ",
 Cell[BoxData["u"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "551c00cf-fc58-99c4-0323-99a8f5d2eb2e"],
 " exactly."
}], "Item",
 CellID->570920987,ExpressionUUID->"22235db8-54be-42b7-53d1-54e25d4b109d"],

Cell["\<\
Three photons in the Fourier tritter populate only the patterns whose mode \
labels add up to a multiple of 3; the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect is the two-photon \
case of the same law. For six photons some patterns the law allows are dark \
as well.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->378517449,ExpressionUUID->"0976d5ae-737d-f257-3f0d-cc080609c0bd"],

Cell["\<\
With one level too few per mode, the tritter either shows patterns the law \
forbids or loses more than half of its probability, depending on how the beam \
splitters are built.\
\>", "Item",
 CellID->1671903560,ExpressionUUID->"13e711b4-4d78-4d68-419c-88fe640d17b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every Fock-space probability equals ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        RowBox[{
         StyleBox["Perm",
          FontSlant->"Plain"], 
         StyleBox["(",
          SpanMaxSize->1], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
           StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
           StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], 
         StyleBox[")",
          SpanMaxSize->1]}]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], "/", 
    StyleBox["\[Product]",
     FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["s", "TI"]}], "!", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Product]",
     FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3fd09d86-aea1-a602-65ef-14e3cb550d68"],
 ", also for inputs with several photons in a mode, and distinguishable \
photons follow ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Perm",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
         RowBox[{
          StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
          StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
    StyleBox["\[Product]",
     FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f6c0922-6605-ed68-5513-a08c13b1b7b2"],
 " instead."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1307059254,ExpressionUUID->"2caab86a-2af9-b1b1-54a9-32344e8d039b"],

Cell["Part III: Boson Sampling with a Random Interferometer", "Section",
 CellID->538512558,ExpressionUUID->"7f56169e-4783-4dbb-256d-8fd872361781"],

Cell["From Galton Boards to Photons: What Boson Sampling Asks", "Subsection",
 CellID->824717693,ExpressionUUID->"5b84d4d6-858d-5842-09bb-cd902c382aa8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Picture a Galton board: balls dropped from the top bounce left or right at \
every peg, and pile up in bins at the bottom. Simulating it is easy: follow \
one ball at a time, flip a coin at every peg, and record the bin it lands in; \
the pile of many balls just adds up these independent single-ball outcomes. \
Distinguishable photons in an interferometer behave exactly like those balls: \
each photon picks its exit port on its own, with the probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[
        RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "67558936-e5eb-8680-0d6a-2173939fecea"],
 ", and the pattern of detections adds up the photons' independent choices. \
Recall that we checked exactly this for three photons: the formula for \
distinguishable photons is the sum over the histories in which each photon \
picks its exit on its own. Identical photons cannot be followed one at a \
time. The amplitude for a detection pattern adds up every way of routing the \
photons to the detected modes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1072dc7c-f7d5-c74e-4001-d6398261ad94"],
 " of them, and these ways interfere, as we saw in the tritter. That sum is \
the permanent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->496527141,ExpressionUUID->"3462f0a3-098c-f6b3-5c11-e90da83edc99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Boson sampling, proposed by ",
 ButtonBox["Aaronson and Arkhipov",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.3245"], None}],
 ", is the task of producing detection patterns with the probabilities of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04cac1af-436c-9192-2cc9-d809761ee3f8"],
 " identical photons sent through an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63be94f2-239e-9b81-1145-0dbc5628e9eb"],
 "-mode interferometer. In other words, a boson sampler is a Galton board for \
identical photons, and the question is whether a classical computer can \
imitate it. Their hardness argument, the evidence that a classical computer \
cannot do this efficiently, takes the interferometer to be chosen at random. \
A random interferometer means a unitary drawn uniformly from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["U", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a3d7a71-218e-1995-0bc3-7c3b503b6bff"],
 " (the Haar measure), which the Wolfram Language samples with ",
 ButtonBox["CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/\
CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution.html"], None}],
 ". Unlike the Fourier matrix, it has no symmetry that could enforce a \
suppression law."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2009363188,ExpressionUUID->"3a0f2024-2f71-09ca-6a34-b98e4a045b10"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Generate a Haar-random ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"6", "\[Times]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "277956ac-4c9d-d338-4d07-4ff66529be02"],
 " unitary with a fixed seed, and verify that it is unitary:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->55669068,ExpressionUUID->"178a6a52-23e4-1142-3d89-8c1c559163a8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2026", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"u6", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", "6", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"UnitaryMatrixQ", "[", "u6", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[62]:= ",
 CellID->1753574084,ExpressionUUID->"52ddf811-e480-8137-02e2-f25a8d3ad01d"],

Cell["\<\
Build the corresponding QuantumFramework interferometer for three photons \
(four levels per mode), and count its gates:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2038359728,ExpressionUUID->"719ae17a-c654-ed44-27b9-f927f3e6b7ae"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sampler", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
    RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"sampler", "[", "\"\<GateCount\>\"", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[63]:= ",
 CellID->1525364821,ExpressionUUID->"62c8f42b-c628-388a-12f7-ee74f3c28ad0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"6", "\[CenterDot]", "5", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36e5ffeb-8179-694d-5e9a-f6b5300c3b97"],
 " beam splitters and the six phase shifters of the mesh."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535108406,ExpressionUUID->"7af061c8-c44a-ae8e-2a80-7895edfcf4d4"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the interferometer's transfer matrix reproduces the random \
unitary to machine precision:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1528788962,ExpressionUUID->"0d437dad-8290-de9a-3b71-74f7372aa4e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"transferMatrix", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
        RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "2"}], 
      "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "u6"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[64]:= ",
 CellID->1505774531,ExpressionUUID->"7aafc905-908a-67da-2a54-e16f213f4d20"],

Cell["\<\
Send three photons into the first three modes, and collect the probability of \
every detection pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->535490749,ExpressionUUID->"62016b94-8ad8-fb56-123e-82de2f52c9bc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"inputPattern", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ",
      "0"}], "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"samplerOut", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"sampler", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"inputPattern", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"probabilities", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KeyMap", "[", 
    RowBox[{"First", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"samplerOut", "[", "\"\<Probability\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[65]:= ",
 CellID->1238905205,ExpressionUUID->"0e7c794a-82c2-56e7-3604-711437773ccd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify that every one of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", "+", "6", "-", "1"}], "3"},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30f601cf-5001-fb68-608d-98a961b5c9b2"],
 " possible patterns occurs:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2125008310,ExpressionUUID->"04bc0f0b-f02f-243d-2c43-a75481db8f07"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "6", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[66]:= ",
 CellID->1684656716,ExpressionUUID->"1a24bdc2-598a-1b95-4bdb-34ac583f69ff"],

Cell["Verify that the output state is normalized:", "Text",
 CellID->2057792111,ExpressionUUID->"705e212e-f5a4-7717-2065-b88bfc515a7d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"samplerOut", "[", "\"\<Norm\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], 
   "]"}], " ", "==", " ", "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[67]:= ",
 CellID->408837332,ExpressionUUID->"5c2f5325-a3f6-c048-05d5-4a8ed5809292"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Here ",
 ButtonBox["Chop",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Chop.html"], None}],
 " sets the tiny machine-precision residue of the norm to zero, so the \
comparison tests the physics rather than the rounding."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1068510841,ExpressionUUID->"211ecaf2-61ee-418f-5725-e3bc179b13d5"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that every probability agrees with the permanent formula:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1027032549,ExpressionUUID->"51e4dffc-d38f-5703-079b-d6b9e63a3a69"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Values", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
         RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "inputPattern", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
        "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "probabilities", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
  " ", "<", " ", 
  RowBox[{"10", "^", 
   RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[68]:= ",
 CellID->171792661,ExpressionUUID->"30e43b5d-74af-d0fb-609b-b3077d5ba2c1"],

Cell["\<\
So the QuantumFramework simulation in Fock space and the permanent formula \
are two representations of the same physics, and they agree to machine \
precision.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->574949478,ExpressionUUID->"44d9380c-2e05-8f35-6ce6-b2564bb1d21f"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the probability of every pattern for distinguishable photons in the \
same interferometer:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1664775781,ExpressionUUID->"36758762-649a-f7b1-5e0a-1f4c0d2cdd9b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"distinguishable", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AssociationMap", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
       RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "inputPattern", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
      "&"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "probabilities", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[69]:= ",
 CellID->884697794,ExpressionUUID->"138e1639-4d05-8b97-41b5-886364b1d9fd"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the probabilities of the patterns for identical and for distinguishable \
photons, sorted by the probability for identical photons:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->784201795,ExpressionUUID->"156728ce-0023-e03b-431c-c1a8b1d7b301"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"order", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Ordering", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Values", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], ",", " ", "All", ",", 
       " ", "Greater"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ListPlot", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Values", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "order", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Values", "[", "distinguishable", "]"}], "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", "order", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<identical photons\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<distinguishable photons\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Large"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<pattern (sorted by the identical-photon probability)\>\"",
         ",", " ", "\"\<probability\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{
     "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
      " ", "\"\<Three photons in a Haar-random six-mode \
interferometer\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[70]:= ",
 CellID->1193259712,ExpressionUUID->"7fc37353-2ed8-42c8-25f1-6b1d4b6d1012"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, identical photons do not follow the distinguishable ones: \
pattern by pattern, interference raises some probabilities above the \
classical value and pushes others below it, and without a symmetry there is \
no simple rule telling which is which. Every probability is its own \
permanent. One rule does survive in every interferometer. When all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26ff5c08-e081-ff27-4e85-56559135c20d"],
 " photons leave through the same mode ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07c988c4-3ef2-8066-2df6-21aeba84d34c"],
 ", the matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
    StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bc0a2f3-6150-447f-79ff-3bbd10e52f45"],
 " has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ac66077-3bfa-1f18-2afe-7a31bd8f6262"],
 " identical rows, so its permanent is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d863d84-94ab-5643-6bbd-b4ee1d5e3ca9"],
 ", while its determinant would vanish. Squaring and dividing by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7ab8b877-e011-189c-2a47-323091a46ae6"],
 " gives ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
     StyleBox["k", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
       {
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
         StyleBox[
          RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
      },
      GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
      GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35eb0178-2238-e094-63e8-992257b2b2fe"],
 " for identical photons, exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0da6433d-a7a4-ba24-3b5e-5b66d256090e"],
 " times the classical value ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
      {
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]]}
     },
     GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
     GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "462f64f6-435d-c7dd-6fd5-7db076e9ad27"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1084903799,ExpressionUUID->"4b06bf63-5f43-ed7c-793d-374d5af7b446"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify, for a general complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"6", "\[Times]", "6"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fd1c247-21a4-d962-35ee-e4215056a848"],
 " matrix and for two to five photons entering the first modes, that every \
fully bunched pattern is exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09347675-9fce-c17b-38cc-683f1a789041"],
 " times more likely for identical photons than for distinguishable ones:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->964492758,ExpressionUUID->"2c597ed5-00d9-d535-5467-779fb16dbc1f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"wGeneral", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalW]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "5"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", " ", 
          RowBox[{"IdentityMatrix", "[", "6", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"bosonProbability", "[", 
             RowBox[{"wGeneral", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}], 
              ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"n", "!"}], " ", 
             RowBox[{"distinguishableProbability", "[", 
              RowBox[{"wGeneral", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                  RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}],
                ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[71]:= ",
 CellID->242210635,ExpressionUUID->"66c4d8d6-27c8-a0db-0efb-d1905262f221"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that returns the total probability of the bunched \
patterns, those with two or more photons in some mode, for identical and for \
distinguishable photons entering the interferometer ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["u", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d3801b6-8b23-0df3-74c7-98f02ed657d9"],
 " with occupations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09816d05-11e9-fb6e-3fbe-856fa79dc9b4"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->360816480,ExpressionUUID->"35ec423d-cde2-7917-6394-6466eb97487d"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "bunchedProbabilities", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"bunchedProbabilities", "[", 
   RowBox[{"u_", ",", " ", "s_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"bunched", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", "s", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "s", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Max", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ">=", " ", "2"}], " ", "&"}]}],
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"f", " ", "|->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"f", "[", 
           RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "s", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
         " ", "/@", " ", "bunched"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"<|", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\"\<identical\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "bosonProbability"}], ",",
         " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<distinguishable\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
         "distinguishableProbability"}]}], "|>"}]}], "]"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[72]:= ",
 CellID->1505759259,ExpressionUUID->"05e0e9bc-56b1-1bf2-339f-00e6634469d8"],

Cell["Compute them for our random interferometer:", "Text",
 CellID->1384053022,ExpressionUUID->"46408f14-a324-388b-6e7f-2751d6d68ad1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bunchedProbabilities", "[", 
  RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "inputPattern"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[73]:= ",
 CellID->1395659232,ExpressionUUID->"40213c85-9219-7c2b-71de-b5ef27ac4771"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this interferometer, as in the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect, identical photons \
prefer to share modes. Is that a property of this particular interferometer? \
Averaged over Haar-random interferometers, the bunching of identical photons \
has an exact answer. The average of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]},
    "Bra"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "678faed4-2cca-f411-0db4-479e457cdf7b"],
 " over the Haar measure commutes with every interferometer, because the \
measure does not change when all its unitaries are multiplied by a fixed one. \
The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b3cac94-919f-f08d-6ac3-45de202bc2d7"],
 "-photon states span a space on which the interferometers act with no \
smaller invariant subspace, so by Schur's lemma that average is the identity \
divided by the dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "634a1270-2707-566e-1149-943a52b23cb4"],
 ": every pattern is equally likely on average. Only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "571f0194-b08e-3ab4-7d24-98d1c138889e"],
 " of the patterns are collision-free, with no mode receiving more than one \
photon, so the average probability of the bunched patterns is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "-", 
   RowBox[{
    TemplateBox[{
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Binomial"], "/", 
    TemplateBox[{
      RowBox[{
        StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
     "Binomial"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "79764466-e076-5945-2f0e-5e4391032baf"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->874592789,ExpressionUUID->"54e8dec7-14b1-519a-7c97-d7a19d4423e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute this average for three photons as a function of the number of modes \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25f5c72f-3423-741a-538a-de89bdd65f60"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1596157938,ExpressionUUID->"6dbbd446-5835-e39a-1b58-ce2059c1b1e0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bunchedAverage", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
       RowBox[{"m", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"m", " ", "+", " ", "2"}], ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"m", " ", ">", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[74]:= ",
 CellID->1496122589,ExpressionUUID->"6d34e655-b983-17e8-14cb-f81f38367d32"],

Cell["Evaluate it for six modes:", "Text",
 CellID->1956327387,ExpressionUUID->"5c435daa-0d1c-c5df-0471-54f4a4aeaf25"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bunchedAverage", " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"m", " ", "->", " ", "6"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[75]:= ",
 CellID->1131177628,ExpressionUUID->"21714cd0-c04e-e57a-570f-659df1f8cc40"],

Cell["\<\
Draw a thousand Haar-random six-mode interferometers and compute the bunched \
probabilities in each (this cell takes a few seconds):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->611195905,ExpressionUUID->"74ff421b-073b-c6d4-1c85-6445b2cfac3e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "2027", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"haarSamples", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"bunchedProbabilities", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", "6", "]"}], "]"}], ",",
        " ", "inputPattern"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "1000"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[76]:= ",
 CellID->1202919897,ExpressionUUID->"3ebc3a74-dd7c-3fa6-6643-bc31d40e858c"],

Cell["Compute the averages over the thousand draws:", "Text",
 CellID->1334651244,ExpressionUUID->"7d5c93fe-a057-3a16-2b63-0abbd1e3897c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "haarSamples", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[77]:= ",
 CellID->185339758,ExpressionUUID->"487dadd0-5ed6-7873-7802-449a5b634b59"],

Cell["Compute the standard errors of these averages:", "Text",
 CellID->1677030473,ExpressionUUID->"5219761b-8a64-c9ff-0227-68452f169bc5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "haarSamples", "]"}], "/", 
  RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "1000", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[78]:= ",
 CellID->134345938,ExpressionUUID->"69346765-6d1c-e9c9-18cc-7f4f04aebb13"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the estimate for identical photons lies within its standard \
error of the exact average, and distinguishable photons land in bunched \
patterns far less often. So bunching is not an accident of one \
interferometer: on average, identical photons share modes more often than \
distinguishable ones.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->350820043,ExpressionUUID->"7c22b8c2-70f4-0562-25d1-31ac00816c48"],

Cell["Sampling: What a Boson Sampler Actually Outputs", "Subsection",
 CellID->456450236,ExpressionUUID->"04fec585-b88c-469b-2c85-dcef39392ce1"],

Cell["\<\
An experiment never shows the probabilities themselves. Each run ends with \
detectors clicking, which yields one pattern; repeating the run produces a \
list of patterns drawn from the distribution above. That list is the output \
of a boson sampler.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1767337052,ExpressionUUID->"7aa617d4-4041-969d-2a5d-8e9e71f5fce7"],

Cell["\<\
Draw ten detection events from the distribution, the record that ten runs of \
the experiment would produce:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1422053341,ExpressionUUID->"5e86e5c8-d785-1389-06bd-fc95e23061d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"RandomChoice", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", "probabilities", "]"}], " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"QuditName", " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "probabilities", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
   "10"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[79]:= ",
 CellID->603286833,ExpressionUUID->"3582ea65-851b-2569-63b1-0c4f2caf8fb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every fresh evaluation of this cell gives a different list, exactly like a \
new batch of runs in the laboratory. The first boson-sampling experiments, \
reported at the end of 2012, worked at the same scale as this example: ",
 ButtonBox["Broome and collaborators",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1231440"], None}],
 " sent two and three photons through a six-mode network, ",
 ButtonBox["Spring and collaborators",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1231692"], None}],
 " three and four photons through a six-mode chip, and ",
 ButtonBox["Tillmann and collaborators",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://doi.org/10.1038/nphoton.2013.102"], None}],
 " three photons through a five-mode circuit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1349832744,ExpressionUUID->"5e81d752-d9a7-cf7a-06be-cf1fd8539240"],

Cell["Part IV: The Classical Cost of Simulating Identical Photons", "Section",
 CellID->16034565,ExpressionUUID->"6dc17641-57cc-3497-1bff-682b627e9efd"],

Cell["\<\
Counting States: The Truncated Fock Space and the Photon Sector\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->344152329,ExpressionUUID->"647a9320-5a37-336f-0c19-0a8a5fc381b5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's recall how QuantumFramework represented the three photons. Every mode \
needed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1", "=", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57b40e76-1aa6-da65-7d4b-a0309f50a94f"],
 " levels, so the state lives in a truncated Fock space of dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["4", "6"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "575b10e3-003a-b957-7d78-89cdb1cc0bbd"],
 ". Because the interferometer conserves photon number, all the amplitude \
stays inside the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c7345dd-208f-a284-2401-5c87513bf0ee"],
 "-photon sector, the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0121a537-2575-8479-30de-3d714c01ef43"],
 " patterns we have been listing, and QuantumFramework stores the state as a \
sparse array holding only those entries."
}], "Text",
 CellID->622383932,ExpressionUUID->"7f325126-465a-e19d-26c2-488073ecb3e7"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the output state stores exactly one amplitude per three-photon \
pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->2102744249,ExpressionUUID->"739af998-c5c1-31b3-21b9-f0c5ec758399"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"samplerOut", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<NonzeroValues\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "6", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[80]:= ",
 CellID->565659401,ExpressionUUID->"003becda-d908-4451-31d8-0587d8bd2ebb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How many modes should we take? Exact sampling means drawing detection \
patterns from the ideal distribution itself; approximate sampling means \
drawing them from some distribution close to it, which is the most a real \
experiment, with its noise and losses, can do. Aaronson and Arkhipov carried \
out their hardness argument for approximate sampling with many modes, of \
order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "5"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["log",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aeb468a-2cc6-59e2-2ae9-5fd445732bc8"],
 ", and they suspect that an improved analysis could bring this down to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3873a668-04d7-31ac-6800-3832ad6383f6"],
 " of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4156c81a-8a68-59d7-776d-e2442f1d2b3d"],
 ". Their argument needs at least that many, because with fewer modes almost \
every detection event puts two photons into the same mode. Recall that, \
averaged over Haar-random interferometers, every pattern of identical photons \
is equally likely, so the average probability of the collision-free patterns \
is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"], "/", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
       StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e7ab4-00f8-e339-7ea6-73feb172ce03"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->561487989,ExpressionUUID->"0b3ec616-de69-0141-3ac5-d853db1c53ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute this probability for as many modes as photons, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c0d57bf-7ae8-3253-2433-4ef97e8280b9"],
 ", as the number of photons grows:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2021628840,ExpressionUUID->"0aaecb0d-dff0-cd78-3a55-e356d98a9442"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
     "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[81]:= ",
 CellID->41425461,ExpressionUUID->"4fe4a286-576e-fd11-759b-3be06218c47b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute it for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07179650-9fbb-2bc1-2d2c-081a1a4e792b"],
 " modes, with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7aecd320-e31f-2936-2a93-ca8d96aa781c"],
 " a positive constant:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208764476,ExpressionUUID->"326b0854-5043-0b63-6268-a21e61f65649"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"c", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}]}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", "n", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",",
       " ", "n"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Assumptions", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"c", " ", ">", " ", "0"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[82]:= ",
 CellID->1584634344,ExpressionUUID->"1d6edc53-4ce5-e0f2-4b15-d61d6491b2d8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So with as many modes as photons almost every detection event has a \
collision, while with a number of modes of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "45f7e4e6-4e1c-a184-738c-fdc06baef3ee"],
 " a fixed fraction of the events stays collision-free, and that fraction \
approaches one as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["c", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "70e98525-204e-6ba4-2096-1c8f51fb398e"],
 " grows. This is why ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "704169dd-a4db-5005-207e-8086cd6e236f"],
 " is the natural scale for the number of modes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->35679398,ExpressionUUID->"7b2d1c14-5aff-cd5f-2ad2-965e5e8b97a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tabulate both counts for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62ac11c1-6d0b-a8c0-1253-88ab04bffa2a"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e7621e1-2fba-a33a-560d-b8cb4a4c0e00"],
 " modes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1113372800,ExpressionUUID->"15938457-0322-a4d9-43a0-1e11b6d40e23"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "^", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], ")"}]}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
        "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<m\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<(n+1)^m\>\"",
         ",", " ", "\"\<Binomial[n+m-1,n]\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[83]:= ",
 CellID->969867355,ExpressionUUID->"7f1ed2e3-b722-4b37-2525-cbccc2d7161d"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the truncated Fock space grows far faster than the photon \
sector, because it reserves room for every mode to hold every photon at once. \
The sparse storage keeps QuantumFramework away from the first count, but it \
still labels each basis state by one index over the whole truncated space.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1210037699,ExpressionUUID->"52e63e44-9d5c-26a1-029d-b02e14ee8c8b"],

Cell["\<\
Check whether the truncated Fock space for five photons in twenty-five modes \
still fits in the range of machine integers used for that index:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1239892393,ExpressionUUID->"6e766a94-5ec6-6187-160d-83de5b7333ed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"5", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "^", "25"}], " ", "<=", " ", 
  "Developer`$MaxMachineInteger"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[84]:= ",
 CellID->1498748757,ExpressionUUID->"2eead67c-41e5-1519-56e9-c82677907c63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This means that at five photons in twenty-five modes the Fock-space state \
cannot even be created, although only ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"29", "5"},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23a655ec-dad2-e192-515e-4cc9df64b3f8"],
 " of its amplitudes would ever be nonzero. The photon sector itself is still \
modest there. We will come back to it by computing the amplitudes in the \
photon sector directly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1701544389,ExpressionUUID->"62ef85cc-c62f-39ac-1294-1ca9f3db8bf6"],

Cell["Timing QuantumFramework as the Photon Number Grows", "Subsection",
 CellID->1682415361,ExpressionUUID->"7d6c313b-6800-4a9b-2b13-a96509b518e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To see how the cost grows, we take ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75dfb56b-bb47-a02b-23e4-2d353ef3f371"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "57533ce7-69d6-be0e-7d60-b5c108600554"],
 " modes, where the truncated space stays indexable up to large ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27c3fefb-2ee6-8038-4df0-f7a54a90d302"],
 ", and time the two stages of the simulation separately: building the mesh \
of beam splitters for a Haar-random unitary, and applying it to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "1"}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "60d4995f-bb7f-b80c-10eb-11193e0b0b56"],
 ". ",
 ButtonBox["MaxMemoryUsed",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/MaxMemoryUsed.html"], 
    None}],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"[", "expr", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64608bbe-760c-8af3-0c1f-22f803bed8d9"],
 " reports the largest amount of memory used while ",
 Cell[BoxData["expr"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09661063-a2cf-675e-3f1d-8a4cd77a4da4"],
 " is evaluated. QuantumFramework also caches the operators it builds, so \
evaluating these timing cells a second time in the same session measures less \
work; to repeat a measurement, start a fresh kernel."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1697357464,ExpressionUUID->"5561d787-26b0-8d0a-031e-cee1534ad450"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that returns, for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0fea91e8-e80e-a1ed-35e9-08b589b8f337"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "37725419-c8bf-c4cd-5d02-4e42e94bae17"],
 " modes, the time to build the interferometer, the time to apply it, and the \
peak memory (in megabytes) used while applying it:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1540797058,ExpressionUUID->"6eee5857-8f9d-bf63-1696-52112a290249"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "qfCost", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"qfCost", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "m_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "apply", "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "m"}], "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
           RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", "m", "]"}], 
           "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"input", " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
               RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}], ",",
             " ", 
            RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
       "   ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
        RowBox[{"With", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"timedBuild", " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
             RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
              RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
           "\n", "    ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
           RowBox[{"With", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"bytes", " ", "=", " ", 
               RowBox[{"MaxMemoryUsed", "[", 
                RowBox[{"apply", " ", "=", " ", 
                 RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
                  RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"Last", "[", "timedBuild", "]"}], "[", "input", 
                    "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"First", "[", "timedBuild", "]"}], ",", " ", "apply", ",",
                " ", 
               RowBox[{"N", "[", 
                RowBox[{"bytes", "/", 
                 RowBox[{"2", "^", "20"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[85]:= ",
 CellID->768596373,ExpressionUUID->"2635f536-2fc9-ab3c-4fca-ed704a7df606"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Measure the cost for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b3760e9-4a32-92b2-4acd-79b36fc4e098"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fe93a8-4ee9-5b9e-3c85-0af26a9c29e4"],
 " modes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "2"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "11"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "11cf5d11-52cc-ddbb-47f5-555b677ea781"],
 " (this cell takes about half a minute):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1985169054,ExpressionUUID->"7ba8138a-66ce-478c-2957-8ad4137b2dd6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"costs", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"qfCost", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "11"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[86]:= ",
 CellID->770675313,ExpressionUUID->"35c9e6d4-f3c4-84c1-63f6-ff918676ee2b"],

Cell["Tabulate the build and apply times:", "Text",
 CellID->846554368,ExpressionUUID->"6fd66644-13e4-6fa7-15ee-782ea591358d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MapThread", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Prepend", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"costs", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{";;", " ", "2"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "11"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<build (s)\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<apply (s)\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[87]:= ",
 CellID->1952818843,ExpressionUUID->"00abf1cf-696b-3507-30a8-e8a9081f9c6d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As you can see, building takes most of the time from three photons on. It \
makes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03d898fe-d35a-9eef-31e7-11bbe6ece435"],
 " beam splitters, each a matrix on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03dda600-4b0b-c3af-31e2-386a6ebf91f5"],
 " levels of its two modes, and its cost grows polynomially. The apply time \
stays small while the photon sector is small and starts to climb only at the \
end of the range. Applying the gates carries the whole photon sector through \
the mesh, and the sector grows by nearly a factor of four with every added \
photon."
}], "Text",
 CellID->599175116,ExpressionUUID->"4de38b79-ee67-8bee-7b90-23228b13d934"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the limit of the ratio of successive sector sizes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]},
    "Binomial"], "/", 
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", 
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
    "Binomial"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "347cf1ed-0cc4-b4dc-5c03-e8b7a5761e26"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234886004,ExpressionUUID->"7d81b9ce-3a4c-aa2a-2bbe-30a8bffef970"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Limit", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", " ", "n"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "n"}], 
     "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"n", " ", "->", " ", "Infinity"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[88]:= ",
 CellID->1955603644,ExpressionUUID->"6bb9b374-9caf-337d-1946-2b3e155b9e47"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Compute the peak memory per amplitude of the photon sector, in bytes, \
dividing by the sector size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", 
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6c340229-13f4-0181-15cb-a473a58153eb"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->529524776,ExpressionUUID->"25dfa134-0866-9bb5-53e4-397ea910e99f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
       RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "11"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"2", "^", "20"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"costs", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
          RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", 
            RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
             RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "11"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",",
           " ", 
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
           RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "11"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<bytes per amplitude\>\""}], 
       "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[89]:= ",
 CellID->186212144,ExpressionUUID->"425139cc-45a5-cefb-726e-b0966c5194c1"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the memory per amplitude falls while the sector is small, \
where a fixed amount of memory dominates, and once the sector passes a few \
thousand amplitudes it stops falling and starts to rise: from there on the \
memory grows at least as fast as the sector does. Extend the range to twelve \
or thirteen photons in a fresh kernel and watch whether the apply time \
overtakes the build time, keeping an eye on the memory.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->284725946,ExpressionUUID->"4d922994-f334-45bb-7ba1-c0d186c12f81"],

Cell["The Same Physics Without the Truncated Fock Space", "Subsection",
 CellID->1006536905,ExpressionUUID->"06c25578-1780-b25e-2ef2-4d22a23a00a4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The truncated Fock space is bookkeeping: the physics lives in the photon \
sector. So let's describe the output state directly there, in plain Wolfram \
Language, in two ways. Both start from one observation: the interferometer \
transforms each creation operator linearly with its transfer matrix, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["U", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f70617e-b140-9f95-0500-793bc0fae5ff"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->207506748,ExpressionUUID->"79d0371a-30a6-04e5-2fef-af4441536ecf"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Let's check this for a single beam splitter, in the untruncated algebra. \
Since ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["G", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d950d76-dd18-2b24-2baa-a533d4ad760e"],
 " with the generator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7234a9f4-3232-6781-23cb-40be47c74deb"],
 " we built earlier, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["B", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["G", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["G", "TI"]}]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], "+", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], ",", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["[",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["G", "TI"], ",", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"]}], 
     StyleBox["]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", "\[Ellipsis]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42668d78-f434-72a4-721d-2525fdc1408e"],
 ". If the commutator with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c7cc198-0ad8-2426-3403-d8c2af528f0c"],
 " maps the two creation operators linearly into each other, the whole series \
is the exponential of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69698b1d-3dc2-3628-1f16-2347b4749d72"],
 " matrix of that linear map."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1146295856,ExpressionUUID->"701e1eb7-eeba-61c8-2025-97f08b4f3312"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the commutators of the generator with the two creation operators:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->438365529,ExpressionUUID->"0e322415-281a-3695-37c1-be5f49ac9cff"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"commutators", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"BosonicNormalOrder", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Commutator", "[", 
       RowBox[{"generator", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "fieldVars", ",",
       " ", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Scalars\>\"", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a1Dag", ",", " ", "a2Dag"}], "}"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[90]:= ",
 CellID->174000849,ExpressionUUID->"61beb272-ef15-9663-1745-343f8aa1fd49"],

Cell["\<\
As one can see, the commutator turns each creation operator into a multiple \
of the other one.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->766726627,ExpressionUUID->"5e8a6a96-06b4-6465-0689-83d0b3414f4f"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the exponential of the matrix of this linear map is the transfer \
matrix of the beam splitter:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1506609767,ExpressionUUID->"55951090-ef25-ccfd-03aa-89dd8ad196c7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"FullSimplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MatrixExp", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Coefficient", "[", 
         RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"a1Dag", ",", " ", "a2Dag"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], 
       " ", "/@", " ", "commutators"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
    RowBox[{"bsBlock", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\[Theta]", ",", " ", "\[Phi]"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{"\[Theta]", " ", "|", " ", "\[Phi]"}], ")"}], " ", "\[Element]", 
    " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[91]:= ",
 CellID->281363281,ExpressionUUID->"53a2ca13-da2c-324e-0151-ec5cdfde8094"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "So a beam splitter rotates the creation operators with its transfer matrix, \
and a mesh of beam splitters composes these rotations into the transfer \
matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["W", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5930221d-821b-4026-08cf-c44737ae130c"],
 " of the whole interferometer. The interferometer also leaves the vacuum \
alone, so the output state is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["k", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      RowBox[{
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
        StyleBox[
         RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}], 
    TemplateBox[{"0"},
     "Ket"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76ba63e9-5df8-c241-1e5a-7ab3547290ab"],
 ", with one factor for each input photon. Creation operators commute with \
each other, so this product is an ordinary polynomial in the variables ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "319e51f9-a9ce-1d21-67a6-48a2c87b640b"],
 " standing for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubsuperscriptBox[
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "^"], 
   StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "26f4962c-805e-a216-4e8b-087631e8f17c"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "=", 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "313d5a7b-7caf-7acc-60c3-5c25755a4816"],
 " applied to the vacuum is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"],
       LimitsPositioning->False], 
      SubscriptBox[
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], "!"}]], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2da78195-91be-94f0-5b5c-18df2048feda"],
 ". In other words, the output amplitude of a pattern is the coefficient of \
its monomial, times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Product]",
      FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "!"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39c6b7ab-78e0-e73c-6ffd-2ef5789aca06"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1615544595,ExpressionUUID->"3f7d0c35-7157-44bf-6502-a67f00e22e85"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that computes all output amplitudes as the coefficients \
of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderoverscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], "=", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   StyleBox["(",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited], 
   UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"j", "k"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    FontSize->1.2 Inherited]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47b49f91-c3c7-4deb-6d4b-16daf6721731"],
 ", for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "064e3005-d89e-7c03-2e75-aa6ed92b4769"],
 " photons entering the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76c2caed-aea0-13a2-1ef1-e3b6cb556188"],
 " modes:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1805673747,ExpressionUUID->"260c3025-1fa9-9acd-4e33-a98f9a5de817"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "polynomialAmplitudes", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"polynomialAmplitudes", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "n_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"x", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[FormalX]", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "w", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    
    RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "->", " ", 
         RowBox[{"#2", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
           RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"#1", "!"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", 
      "@@@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"CoefficientRules", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
         RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"x", " ", ".", " ", 
            RowBox[{"w", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", 
              RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", 
               RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}], 
         "]"}], ",", " ", "x"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[92]:= ",
 CellID->1547520620,ExpressionUUID->"4b1e6c2c-0452-4134-7925-8676ade7101e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Verify, for a general symbolic ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Times]", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2982aea8-af87-65d7-5fb1-47f5ca324f3d"],
 " matrix, that the coefficient of every pattern of four photons in four \
modes gives the permanent formula:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->858350929,ExpressionUUID->"19ac3a5e-0cd6-873c-4f53-bc18a560ea06"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"wGeneral", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Array", "[", 
      RowBox[{"\[FormalW]", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"amps", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"polynomialAmplitudes", "[", 
        RowBox[{"wGeneral", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
     
     RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
        RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Expand", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"amps", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
             RowBox[{"wGeneral", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Range", "[", "4", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
            
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
             RowBox[{"Times", " ", "@@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"#", "!"}], ")"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], " ", "===", " ",
          "0"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[93]:= ",
 CellID->2138894257,ExpressionUUID->"6e8690e9-968f-68b3-16bd-09b3233a3a99"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that it reproduces every QuantumFramework amplitude of the six-mode \
example:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1941039383,ExpressionUUID->"2b6bc1ec-c569-bd9f-5968-d8c9ec1d07e5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"amps", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"polynomialAmplitudes", "[", 
       RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"samplerOut", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"amps", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"v", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
             RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
        "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Keys", "[", "amps", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[94]:= ",
 CellID->1670620029,ExpressionUUID->"25f1a39a-81e0-db80-538e-3ac4379aa9ea"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The second way is the first-quantized picture: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35466be2-b7a8-26dc-637d-82cfc2428c26"],
 " identical photons form a totally symmetric wavefunction of rank ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58bdea72-0ba3-5f4c-0842-0c3cae562596"],
 " over the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e8cef58-e908-949c-16b3-070588a2fee6"],
 " modes. Its component at mode labels ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], "1"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0abc4047-6c7b-4886-3a44-5a21050e1aec"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Perm",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["S", "TI"]}]], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "24e21d63-fe6b-5877-4c91-954cfb1e2b5d"],
 " for the pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "348d2737-4aeb-e3cb-5cb2-bf716e9fb111"],
 " those labels describe (with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["S", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2161c865-0900-0907-571e-e24fa8b5586d"],
 " one photon in each of the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3cadbe4b-a339-c651-6452-3014d6cdacbb"],
 " modes), and the factor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!"}]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31169419-f57b-983b-672d-0e42fc0feb01"],
 " normalizes it over all ordered lists of labels. A symmetric tensor is \
fixed by its components with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "1"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], "2"], "\[LessEqual]", "\[Ellipsis]", "\[LessEqual]", 
   
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "40aa99e8-53bd-499c-70a9-10b266481be6"],
 ", one for each pattern, and the Wolfram Language represents exactly this \
with the structured array ",
 ButtonBox["SymmetrizedArray",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/SymmetrizedArray.html"], 
    None}],
 ": given a rule for the components and the symmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Symmetric", "[", "All", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d165407-aaf3-867b-0b2e-4e60ce87ed41"],
 ", it evaluates the rule once per independent component and stores nothing \
else."
}], "Text",
 CellID->588214459,ExpressionUUID->"75cb8946-a0dc-0da7-23c8-2123d169578d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define the symmetric wavefunction of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "63688a50-35e7-99e6-1117-2c1a4393ebcc"],
 " photons entering the first ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12187c95-2034-8b29-4238-75df51c6d673"],
 " modes as a ",
 Cell[BoxData["SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34b193bd-0a67-a7a6-5c4e-0ae7af130d8c"],
 ", whose independent components are permanents:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1759496502,ExpressionUUID->"4fca8ec2-4b73-3b52-75c9-27ac6e0789b8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "symmetricAmplitudes", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"symmetricAmplitudes", "[", 
   RowBox[{"w_", ",", " ", "n_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"SymmetrizedArray", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", "j__", "}"}], " ", ":>", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
       RowBox[{"w", "[", 
        RowBox[{"[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", "j", "}"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Range", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
      RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
       RowBox[{"n", "!"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Length", "[", "w", "]"}], ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Symmetric", "[", "All", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[95]:= ",
 CellID->1641757231,ExpressionUUID->"656925a1-dac3-d209-1316-bc0adf77a153"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that a symmetric tensor of rank 3 over six modes has exactly one \
independent component per three-photon pattern:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->896279625,ExpressionUUID->"09e13884-5cc5-f650-3f9e-b1ee5571dcba"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Length", "[", 
   RowBox[{"SymmetrizedIndependentComponents", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"6", ",", " ", "6", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Symmetric", "[", "All", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Binomial", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"3", " ", "+", " ", "6", " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "3"}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[96]:= ",
 CellID->1264190945,ExpressionUUID->"29829495-262a-abaa-5fb1-0ddf53dcf9f0"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that the wavefunction of the six-mode example is normalized over all \
ordered lists of labels:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1806910998,ExpressionUUID->"136212ad-a4c2-b9f3-4111-8bf6cd740bd9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Chop", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
        RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
         RowBox[{"symmetricAmplitudes", "[", 
          RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", 
      "2"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[97]:= ",
 CellID->962064851,ExpressionUUID->"67f6b273-a0bf-ee61-0d8d-343cd14bb54b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07a2a6c0-d7ac-3784-2d51-3fade25e9dee"],
 " is described by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!", "/", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Product]",
     FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "!"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d29df82-54ab-6c21-24d6-d6ec5d5e370b"],
 " ordered lists of labels, the multinomial coefficient that ",
 ButtonBox["Multinomial",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/Multinomial.html"], None}],
 " computes, so its Fock amplitude is the component times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "!", "/", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Product]",
      FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "!"}]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2673b224-f5d9-a24c-4e00-2b81fc6df096"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1660212291,ExpressionUUID->"27388ee6-22a7-f122-4ec7-27c05753c008"],

Cell["\<\
Verify that this reproduces every QuantumFramework amplitude of the six-mode \
example:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1553450743,ExpressionUUID->"51cd4bfd-d3fa-9dcf-07f3-62a6e58ce715"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"With", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"sa", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"symmetricAmplitudes", "[", 
       RowBox[{"u6", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"v", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"samplerOut", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"sa", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", 
             RowBox[{"Sequence", " ", "@@", " ", 
              RowBox[{"modeList", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Multinomial", " ", "@@", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], " ", "-", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"v", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"fockIndex", "[", 
             RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "4"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
        "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"photonPatterns", "[", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "<", " ", 
    RowBox[{"10", "^", 
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[98]:= ",
 CellID->376345483,ExpressionUUID->"06a776cb-b9d0-3c58-2e5d-6f95386a86a2"],

Cell["\<\
Now let's time the three methods on the same interferometers, with few \
photons in many modes and with as many photons as modes. The QuantumFramework \
time includes building the gates, as before.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1917523023,ExpressionUUID->"7641b941-63e8-8619-1e7e-312b1582ed63"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that times each method on a Haar-random interferometer \
for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42b8cf72-fa81-ffe6-7247-e73fff35c5cc"],
 " photons in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c8db7a0-3aa3-299f-44b2-2e0abf567be5"],
 " modes, skipping QuantumFramework where its Fock-space index would overflow:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->225924774,ExpressionUUID->"473593be-64fb-e664-6eca-0af80c8fcd4e"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "methodTimes", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"methodTimes", "[", 
   RowBox[{"n_", ",", " ", "m_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "u", "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", 
      RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"100", " ", "m"}]}], "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"u", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
       RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", "m", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
     ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"If", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "^", "m"}], " ", ">", 
          " ", "Developer`$MaxMachineInteger"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<TooLarge\>\"", "]"}], ",", "\n", 
         "     ", 
         RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
          RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"interferometer", "[", 
             RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"FockState", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"PadRight", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"ConstantArray", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "m"}], "]"}], 
              ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"n", " ", "+", " ", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], 
        "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
         RowBox[{"polynomialAmplitudes", "[", 
          RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
       RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
         RowBox[{"symmetricAmplitudes", "[", 
          RowBox[{"u", ",", " ", "n"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}]}], 
   "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[99]:= ",
 CellID->1508526016,ExpressionUUID->"79a8e286-b760-8808-2f57-fbe3c21adb52"],

Cell["\<\
Time the three methods (in seconds) for four photons in sixteen modes, five \
photons in twenty-five modes, eight photons in eight modes, and ten photons \
in ten modes (this cell takes about a minute):\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1653333794,ExpressionUUID->"766f3dde-6e6e-8ae3-1e14-b4980b18d8c9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TableForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
      RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"methodTimes", " ", "@@", " ", "#"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ",
     "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"4", ",", " ", "16"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", "25"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"10", ",", " ", "10"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"TableHeadings", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<m\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<QuantumFramework\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<polynomial\>\"", ",", 
        " ", "\"\<SymmetrizedArray\>\""}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[100]:= ",
 CellID->2117504204,ExpressionUUID->"7acff19c-f8f8-c05b-2af4-e8d9f97292a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, with few photons in many modes, the regime of the hardness \
argument, both the polynomial expansion and the ",
 Cell[BoxData["SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "36bb0aa4-099e-3511-5e58-a30ea8289c7b"],
 " beat QuantumFramework by orders of magnitude, and they handle five photons \
in twenty-five modes, where the Fock-space index overflows. There the photon \
sector is small, while QuantumFramework still builds all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fab4322-7f5b-c123-15a9-5a8c7aef9009"],
 " beam splitters, each on the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "559c0528-76f1-864e-03a3-9d720285ec94"],
 " levels of its two modes, however few photons there are. As the number of \
photons approaches the number of modes, the gap narrows: the photon sector \
becomes large, QuantumFramework's sparse state carries it through the mesh \
efficiently once the gates are built, and at ten photons in ten modes the ",
 Cell[BoxData["SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c3b3e9a-7f95-6e09-75d8-b7c47a203553"],
 " falls behind both, because it computes one full permanent for every \
pattern while the polynomial expansion shares partial products between \
patterns. So the representation matters by orders of magnitude, but no \
representation removes the growth of the photon sector: every method that \
produces the whole distribution handles all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", 
      StyleBox["m", "TI"], "-", "1"}], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]},
   "Binomial"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b834648-1855-f17e-29b1-581299e1c044"],
 " amplitudes."
}], "Text",
 CellID->201091240,ExpressionUUID->"6aa15cf4-f328-f435-1a5f-55b186c2df1f"],

Cell["\<\
One Amplitude Is One Permanent: Why the Cost Doubles with Every Photon\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->667003370,ExpressionUUID->"1fa3178e-7287-38be-4550-8ee807338a84"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Suppose we give up on the whole distribution and ask for a single \
probability. Even then we need a permanent. Computing the permanent is \
#P-complete already for matrices of zeros and ones, a 1979 theorem of Valiant \
on which ",
 ButtonBox["Aaronson and Arkhipov",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.3245"], None}],
 " build, and #P-complete problems are believed to be far beyond efficient \
computation. ",
 Cell[BoxData["Permanent"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33c53063-afff-c489-61fa-aa4cc98baed3"],
 " offers several exact methods, among them Ryser's formula, which adds up \
one term for each subset of the columns, and Glynn's formula, which adds up \
one term for each pattern of signs. The cost of both grows like ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "08d8bcb3-70a4-55b3-38e7-35fd01513f99"],
 " times a polynomial in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "20e38226-5aed-155d-5090-1b805e987fa7"],
 "; Aaronson and Arkhipov quote about ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["2", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "160727ef-d1b8-0069-3e3c-bec8e04d52b3"],
 " floating-point operations for Ryser's algorithm. Let's measure Glynn's \
formula."
}], "Text",
 CellID->526043023,ExpressionUUID->"261df1b1-b81e-57af-4e22-e8fb39ab3df5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Define a function that times Glynn's formula for the permanent of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00ba9d2f-c328-50fc-3059-1488f6dd22c6"],
 " block of a Haar-random ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02964792-f196-8b6e-32ae-5edf8020d9b4"],
 "-mode unitary, the matrix behind one output amplitude of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166d4e5f-4333-9385-3e13-601976c7e1ef"],
 " photons, using ",
 ButtonBox["RepeatedTiming",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/RepeatedTiming.html"], 
    None}],
 ", which evaluates an expression several times and returns a trimmed mean of \
the times:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1120596176,ExpressionUUID->"1c99ee20-d785-d362-44a6-078de231be48"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", "permanentTime", "]"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"permanentTime", "[", "n_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", "a", "}"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "n", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{"CircularUnitaryMatrixDistribution", "[", 
         RowBox[{"n", "^", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{";;", " ", "n"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{";;", " ", "n"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", "\n", "  ", 
     RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"RepeatedTiming", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Permanent", "[", 
        RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Method", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<Glynn\>\""}]}], "]"}], 
       "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[101]:= ",
 CellID->64105026,ExpressionUUID->"60858f89-56d8-6615-10ba-26d3636d4d7f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Time it for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "=", "10"}], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "24"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2e45545e-c429-efe4-567b-4e1bedddb5ce"],
 " photons (this cell takes about a minute):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1373525465,ExpressionUUID->"24564246-a2b2-7a9b-4c6e-6423d74748e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"permanentTimes", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"permanentTime", "[", "n", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"n", ",", " ", "10", ",", " ", "24"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[102]:= ",
 CellID->1964307623,ExpressionUUID->"273d1382-afb1-09c0-4ec2-8aefca445b2a"],

Cell["Plot the timings on a logarithmic scale:", "Text",
 CellID->39040159,ExpressionUUID->"39c9e52f-ed06-87fb-6ff6-fc8884b0edc1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLogPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"permanentTimes", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Joined", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotMarkers", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "2"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "Large"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<photons n\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<seconds\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",",
    "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<Time to compute one n\[Times]n permanent\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[103]:= ",
 CellID->1242473813,ExpressionUUID->"46be6341-4be3-06d9-6e46-7b2b6d966c23"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the points fall on a straight line, and on a logarithmic \
scale a straight line means that the time grows exponentially with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "352b8971-1d3f-d4c9-6328-213b94cbbe13"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->290269587,ExpressionUUID->"227c7e4b-1c68-aac8-5204-70159502f812"],

Cell["\<\
Compute the average factor by which the time grows with each added photon, as \
the geometric mean over all fourteen steps:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->471335900,ExpressionUUID->"6cd9b5a9-dbed-51da-14e6-2cf2dd982320"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"permanentTimes", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/", 
    RowBox[{"permanentTimes", "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "^", 
  RowBox[{"(", 
   RowBox[{"1", "/", "14"}], ")"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[104]:= ",
 CellID->1843091513,ExpressionUUID->"4becebe3-5bfe-fac0-7993-02cd5d88c82a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Therefore, every added photon roughly doubles the cost of a single \
amplitude, as the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox["2", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "312d182f-c6c7-5e1e-60d2-9188f3722564"],
 " growth of Ryser's and Glynn's formulas predicts. At that rate, fifty \
photons would put one amplitude far beyond any practical waiting time on a \
laptop, and a hundred photons beyond any computer. This is also why the exact \
sampling algorithm of ",
 ButtonBox["Clifford and Clifford (2018)",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.01260"], None}],
 ", which draws each sample through a chain of conditional probabilities \
without ever computing the whole distribution, still pays about the price of \
two ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Times]", 
   StyleBox["n", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1449d45f-8382-90b9-3c76-ce193634e283"],
 " permanents for every sample it draws, when the number of modes grows \
polynomially with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "444f09dd-766a-dba7-6c74-a087031ca98d"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1978684664,ExpressionUUID->"79e9b65a-67eb-1624-2f96-2804119e7d0e"],

Cell["Permanents Versus Determinants: Why Fermions Are Easy", "Subsection",
 CellID->2064137570,ExpressionUUID->"394df0e2-3b3f-7a44-6f72-e9ccbeca48ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Recall that two identical fermions have the determinant, not the permanent, \
as their amplitude. The two definitions differ only in the signs of the \
terms, yet the signs change everything: the alternating signs let the \
determinant be computed by Gaussian elimination, in a number of operations of \
order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d3de1d4-e864-19c9-04c2-f89189116b13"],
 ", while no such shortcut is known for the permanent."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1265784226,ExpressionUUID->"1adc8861-0296-99d3-4ae3-224bb720eb39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Time the determinant of a random complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1000", "\[Times]", "1000"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "47f3727e-1788-b883-6d81-7438a2220ae9"],
 " matrix:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->872599864,ExpressionUUID->"02bfa0ec-e0fe-2fa7-3244-39c9908b758d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"a", " ", "=", " ", 
     RowBox[{"RandomComplex", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "1"}], " ", "-", " ", "I"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", "I"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1000", ",", " ", "1000"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ClearSystemCache", "[", "]"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"First", " ", "@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"AbsoluteTiming", "[", 
      RowBox[{"Det", "[", "a", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[105]:= ",
 CellID->2056057710,ExpressionUUID->"7cc1833e-1ead-5711-24fe-1b789b583a7b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "As one can see, the amplitude of a thousand identical fermions costs less \
than the permanent of two dozen photons we timed above. As ",
 ButtonBox["Aaronson and Arkhipov",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.3245"], None}],
 " point out, this is why noninteracting fermions are easy to simulate \
classically: the determinant can be computed efficiently, while the permanent \
is #P-complete. For identical photons they showed that an efficient classical \
algorithm sampling exactly from the output distribution would collapse the \
polynomial hierarchy to its third level, a consequence complexity theorists \
consider very unlikely, and that the same holds even for approximate sampling \
from random interferometers with many modes, if two conjectures about \
permanents of Gaussian random matrices hold. The only difference between the \
two particles is one sign under exchange."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1360523735,ExpressionUUID->"3cb4236e-91b2-9328-644b-bb482044fe72"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us (and What Comes Next)", "Subsection",
 CellID->676766013,ExpressionUUID->"631da35c-735e-7e3b-1122-3b0606eb4501"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "You now have a complete, computation-first toolkit for boson sampling: Fock \
states and beam splitters in QuantumFramework, together with its symbolic \
algebra of ladder operators, the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect and its dip as the \
photons become distinguishable, the truncation rule of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44b7daea-ed84-b50e-6c4c-d3b784361c54"],
 " levels per mode, the Reck decomposition that builds any interferometer \
from beam splitters and phase shifters, the suppression law of the Fourier \
interferometer and the dark patterns it misses, the permanent formula for \
every detection probability, sampling from a random interferometer and the \
exact Haar average of bunching, two descriptions of the same output state \
that live in the photon sector alone (a polynomial in creation operators and \
a ",
 Cell[BoxData["SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "39f2334d-24de-3dcb-6f81-ab174d688711"],
 " of permanents), and the three growing costs: the truncated Fock space, the \
photon sector, and the permanent behind every single amplitude. With these \
ideas unified, the notebook's message becomes practical: the physics of \
identical photons is simple to state and simple to simulate for a few \
photons, and the same interference that makes the photons bunch is what makes \
them expensive to imitate. From here, the most natural continuations are \
Gaussian boson sampling, where squeezed light replaces single photons \
(QuantumFramework's ",
 Cell[BoxData["SqueezeOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1ec600b7-0050-8550-46fd-99f1b1eaefba"],
 " is the starting point) and hafnians replace permanents; realistic \
imperfections such as photon loss and partial distinguishability, which we \
met briefly through the polarization angle \[Chi]; and the validation of \
boson samplers, where suppression laws like the one we found for the tritter \
help certify that an experiment behaves quantum mechanically."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1428640414,ExpressionUUID->"33bfe66e-cd59-d601-6144-f84be4edbd6b"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"6a3ee8c1-8740-e1ad-1bc5-01ab32fab3f7"
]
